{"row_id": "q031", "objective": "SPR2015 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) animal models", "anchors": ["SPR2015"], "facet": "readout", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 5770, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://www.genengnews.com/topics/cancer/merck-scibrunch-launch-up-to-2-13b-collaboration-to-develop-preclinical-kras-inhibiting-molecular-glue/", "domain": "genengnews.com", "title": "Merck, SciBrunch Launch Up-to-$2.13B Collaboration ...", "date": "2026-09-29", "text": "At the 2026 American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) Annual Meeting, a team of SciBrunch researchers that included founder, chairman, and CEO Tao Hu, PhD, presented preclinical data showing SPR2015 to have demonstrated what it termed compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple *in vivo* cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX and PDX) models. ... In a head-to-head mouse study comparing a single oral once-daily dose at 100 mg/kg of SPR2015 to another unspecified G12D (ON) inhibitor in over 15 CRC CDX or PDX models, SPR2015 showed significantly superior efficacy in the *in vivo* CRC xenograft models, achieving a 64.7% objective response rate (ORR) and 94.1% disease control rate (DCR) as monotherapy."}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://trial.medpath.com/organization/revolution-medicines", "domain": "trial.medpath.com", "title": "Revolution Medicines - MedPath Trial", "date": "2026-09-28", "text": "- SPR2015 is a molecular glue inhibitor that showed nanomolar antiproliferative activity in KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines with selectivity over KRAS wild-type cells, plus monotherapy antitumor activity in xenograft models."}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://www.pharmtech.com/view/kras-g12d-inhibitor-s-2-13b-deal-tests-cross-border-tech-transfer", "domain": "pharmtech.com", "title": "KRAS G12D Inhibitor's $2.13B Deal Tests Cross-Border Tech Transfer", "date": "2026-09-28", "text": "- SPR2015 functions as an ON-state molecular glue, showing nanomolar antiproliferative activity in KRAS G12D cell lines with wild-type selectivity and tumor regression in xenograft models. ... SPR2015 is described as a molecular glue inhibitor that engages the ON form of the mutant protein.^1^ It showed nanomolar antiproliferative activity across multiple KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines while maintaining selectivity over wild-type cells, and it demonstrated monotherapy antitumor efficacy in cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models."}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://pharmaphorum.com/news/msd-takes-400m-bite-scibrunchs-kras-drug", "domain": "pharmaphorum.com", "title": "MSD takes a $400m bite of SciBrunch's KRAS drug", "date": "2026-10-02", "text": "The company reported studies at this year's American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) congress which showed antitumour efficacy for SPR2015 as a monotherapy across multiple *in vivo* cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models."}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://www.pharmexec.com/view/merck-licenses-preclinical-kras-g12d-inhibitor-scibrunch", "domain": "pharmexec.com", "title": "Merck Licenses Preclinical KRAS G12D Inhibitor from SciBrunch", "date": "2026-09-28", "text": "KRAS G12D is the most common oncogenic RAS mutation found in human tumors, arising from a substitution of glycine with aspartate at position 12, a change that leaves KRAS active and continuously signaling for cell proliferation and survival.^1^ SPR2015 has also shown compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models, according to preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.^2^"}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://www.merck.com/news/merck-enters-into-exclusive-global-license-agreement-with-scibrunch-therapeutics-for-spr2015-an-investigational-oral-kras-g12d-on-inhibitor/", "domain": "merck.com", "title": "Merck Enters into Exclusive Global License Agreement ...", "date": "2026-10-02", "text": "In addition, SPR2015 has demonstrated compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX/PDX) models, as reported in preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting."}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://x.com/Aiims1742/status/2104884186620494308", "domain": "x.com", "title": "Anirban Maitra on X: \"This #AACR26 abstract is worth $400 ...", "date": "2026-09-29", "text": "Abstract 5978: SPR2015, a highly potent and selective KRAS G12D (on) inhibitor, exhibits favorable..."}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://chemxplore.com/news/merck-scibrunch-spr2015-kras-g12d-license", "domain": "chemxplore.com", "title": "Merck licenses SPR2015, an oral KRAS G12D inhibitor, from ...", "date": "2026-09-28", "text": "- SPR2015 is a preclinical oral KRAS G12D (ON) molecular‑glue inhibitor showing nanomolar antiproliferative activity and monotherapy efficacy in CDX and PDX models. ... SPR2015 is an investigational preclinical oral KRAS G12D (ON) molecular‑glue inhibitor that has demonstrated nanomolar antiproliferative activity in various KRAS G12D‑mutant cell lines with good selectivity over KRAS wild‑type cells. It has shown antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell‑derived and patient‑derived xenograft (CDX/PDX) models, with preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://novapharmanews.com/apac/news/spr2015-merck-400m-2-13b-license", "domain": "novapharmanews.com", "title": "SPR2015: Merck Pays $400M, Up to $2.13B - novapharmanews.com", "date": "2026-09-29", "text": "- SPR2015 is still preclinical. The release cites nanomolar cell-line activity and tumor activity in xenograft models shown at AACR 2026, without a response rate. ... It also cites antitumor activity as a single agent in cell-derived and patient-derived xenografts, from preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR meeting. No tumor-shrinkage percentage is printed."}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://www.lqventures.com/merck-scibrunch-spr2015-deal-diligence-brief/amp/", "domain": "lqventures.com", "title": "Merck–SciBrunch SPR2015 Deal | Lucid Diligence Brief - LucidQuest", "date": "2026-09-29", "text": "SciBrunch’s AACR 2026 abstract described it as IND-enabling and projected Phase 1 entry by the end of 2026. (AACR abstract 5978, Reuters)"}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7621, "cached_input_tokens": 5945, "output_tokens": 536}, "timing": {"search_ms": 747.0, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 7009.3, "total_ms": 7756.3}, "luna_wall_ms": 7009.3, "cost_usd": {"search": 0.001, "jev": 0.0, "luna": 0.0}, "output": {"has_answer": "no", "summarized_answer": "", "missing": "Whether SPR2015 demonstrated tumour growth inhibition, regression or shrinkage specifically in PDAC animal models; the PDAC model identities and any quantitative efficacy results, doses or schedules.", "citations": [], "next_queries": ["SPR2015 PDAC xenograft tumour regression in vivo"]}, "raw_text": null, "metrics": {"json_valid": true, "has_answer": false, "answer_chars": 0, "confident_score": null, "missing_nothing": false, "missing_empty": false, "n_tags": 0, "invalid_tags": [], "uncited_answer": false, "n_cited_items": 0, "cited_domains": [], "url_in_answer": false, "search_talk": [], "nonempty_when_no": false, "claim_tokens": 0, "ungrounded_tokens": [], "n_ungrounded": 0, "names_subject": false, "subject_in_cited": false, "next_queries": 1, "next_queries_subject_first": 1}}
{"row_id": "q030", "objective": "SGR-4174 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma animal models", "anchors": ["SGR-4174"], "facet": "readout", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 10719, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12943-026-02632-7?error=cookies_not_supported&code=89f85997-69de-41bd-b40a-f6985ed2b656", "domain": "link.springer.com", "title": "SOS1: tracking the evolving path from promising to actionable ...", "date": null, "text": "In vivo assays demonstrated that in monotherapy, BI-3406-mediated SOS1 inhibition (50 mg/kg; bid; 21 days) resulted in potent tumor volume reduction in certain KRAS oncogenic xenograft models including G12C (PDAC: Mia PaCa-2), G12S (NSCLC: A549), G12V (PDAC: PATX53; CRC: SW620), and G13D (CRC: LoVo) [39]. ... In vivo studies showed that single-agent administration (100 mg/kg; q.d; 21 days) inhibited tumor growth in a PDAC KRAS^G12C^ mutated model (Mia PaCa-2) but not in the KRAS^G12C^ CRC (SW837) or the KRAS^G12D^ PDAC (AsPC-1) models. ... Oral administration of HW071021 as a single-agent significantly caused TGI (78%) in a murine xenograft model of KRAS^G12C^-driven oncogenicity (Mia PaCa-2 cells) [79]. ... Mechanistically, SGR-4174 binds to the catalytic domain of SOS1, disrupting SOS1::KRAS^G12C^ PPI (IC~50~ of 13 nM) [80]. Preclinical in vitro studies demonstrated that SGR-4174 administration (IC~50~ values ranging from 42 to107 nM) resulted in a robust impairment of RAS-mediated signal transduction and reduced cell viability (3D cell cultures) across a wide spectrum of human cancer cell lines harboring KRAS^G12C/D/V^ or EGFR mutations (since we had no access to the panel of the specific cells employed in this study, this information is not included in Supplementary Table 2) [80]. In KRAS^G12C^-mutated tumor xenograft models, including NSCLC and PDAC, single-agent administration of SGR-4174 elicited dose-dependent TGI (please note that we were unable to find the precise dosing regimens employed in this study) [80]. In addition, concomitant administration of SGR-4174 and Sotorasib resulted in a deeper and more sustained inhibition of KRAS signal transmission, pronounced inhibition of cell proliferation in 3D cell culture models, and tumor regression in xenograft models when compared to the respective monotherapies [80]. Furthermore, along with Trametinib, SGR-4174 prevented the reactivation of the KRAS pathway, which is typically observed upon MEK inhibition, leading to increased tumor cell death and stasis [80]."}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/organization/ee6d0cc13d500f7740bc81b30e6d5978", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "Schrödinger, Inc. - Drug pipelines, Patents, Clinical trials", "date": null, "text": "In KRAS G12C tumor xenograft mouse models, SGR-4174 monotherapy demonstrated dose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and a decrease in the tumor PD biomarker pERK.SGR-4174 was examined in combination with KRAS G12C inhibitor sotorasib and MEK inhibitor trametinib in vitro and in vivo. When combined with sotorasib, SGR-4174 demonstrated deeper and more sustained inhibition of the KRAS signaling pathway, stronger suppression of cell proliferation in 3D cell culture, and tumor regression in xenograft models compared to single agent activity. ... Compared to other published SOS1 inhibitors (BI-3406, MRTX0902), SGR-4174 is more potent, and demonstrated similar anti-tumor activity and target engagement at a lower dose both in monotherapy and combination therapy studies in xenograft tumor models. SGR-4174 was well tolerated as monotherapy and in combination with sotorasib or trametinib.SGR-4174 demonstrated favorable PK properties across preclinical species and toxicity profile was well characterized."}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1186/s12943-026-02632-7.pdf?error=cookies_not_supported&code=aa72aed6-b31a-4006-88df-722541dec95c", "domain": "link.springer.com", "title": "SOS1: tracking the evolving path from promising to actionable ...", "date": null, "text": "In vivo studies showed that single-agent administra­ tion (100 mg/kg; q.d; 21 days) inhibited tumor growth in a PDAC KRASG12C mutated model (Mia PaCa-2) but not in the KRASG12C CRC (SW837) or the KRASG12D PDAC (AsPC-1) models. ... Oral administration of HW071021 as a single-agent significantly caused TGI (78%) in a murine xenograft model of KRASG12C-driven oncogenicity (Mia PaCa-2 cells) [79]. ... SGR-4174 appears as a novel, potent, and highly selec­ … ... Mechanistically, SGR- 4174 binds to the catalytic domain of SOS1, disrupting SOS1::KRASG12C PPI (IC50 of 13 nM) [80]. ... graft models, including NSCLC and PDAC, single-agent administration of SGR-4174 elicited dose-dependent TGI (please note that we were unable to find the pre­ cise dosing regimens employed in this study) [80]. In addition, concomitant administration of SGR-4174 and"}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=1b3e9eec-7ffe-4dfd-8404-27376217e477", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "title": "SGR-4174 / Schrodinger - Larvol Delta", "date": null, "text": "## Preclinical characterization of SGR-4174, a potent and selective SOS1 inhibitor for the treatment of pan KRAS mutant cancers in combination with KRAS pathway inhibitors (AACR 2025) - \"Compared to other published SOS1 inhibitors (BI-3406, MRTX0902), SGR-4174 is more potent, and demonstrated similar anti-tumor activity and target engagement at a lower dose both in monotherapy and combination therapy studies in xenograft tumor models. SGR-4174 was well tolerated as monotherapy and in combination with sotorasib or trametinib.SGR-4174 demonstrated favorable PK properties across preclinical species and toxicity profile was well characterized. Our comprehensive preclinical efficacy and safety data support progressing SGR-4174 to clinical development to treat KRAS mutant cancers.\" ... ## Schrödinger Presents New Preclinical Data at AACR Annual Meeting (Businesswire) - \"SGR-4174 Data at AACR: The poster (Abstract #4376)...includes preclinical data demonstrating the superior binding, selectivity, and drug-like properties of SGR-4147 compared to MRTX0902 as assessed via comprehensive in vitro potency, ADME, and safety assays. The preclinical data for SGR-4174 also show robust suppression of the RAS signaling pathway and potent cell killing activity across multiple cancer types harboring diverse KRAS mutations as well as EGFR and SOS1 mutations. SGR-4174 monotherapy achieved dose-dependent target engagement and tumor growth inhibition and induced tumor shrinkage when used in combination with MEK or KRAS inhibitors in preclinical models of pancreatic and non-small cell lung cancer.\""}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://s203.q4cdn.com/609444515/files/doc_news/Schrdinger-Presents-New-Preclinical-Data-at-AACR-Annual-Meeting-2025.pdf", "domain": "s203.q4cdn.com", "title": "[PDF] Schrödinger Presents New Preclinical Data at AACR Annual Meeting", "date": null, "text": "The data also demonstrated that SGR-4174 has strong tumor growth inhibition as a monotherapy as well as in combination with MEK or KRAS inhibitors, while maintaining a favorable safety pro�le. ... The poster (Abstract #4376), “Preclinical characterization of SGR-4174, a potent and selective SOS1 inhibitor for the treatment of pan KRAS mutant cancers in combination with KRAS pathway inhibitors,” includes preclinical data demonstrating the superior binding, selectivity, and drug-like properties of SGR-4147 compared to MRTX0902 as assessed via comprehensive in vitro potency, ADME, and safety assays. The preclinical data for SGR-4174 also show robust suppression of the RAS signaling pathway and potent cell killing activity across multiple cancer types harboring diverse KRAS mutations as well as EGFR and SOS1 mutations. SGR-4174 monotherapy achieved dose- dependent target engagement and tumor growth inhibition and induced tumor shrinkage when used in combination with MEK or KRAS inhibitors in preclinical models of pancreatic and non-small cell lung cancer."}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://s203.q4cdn.com/609444515/files/doc_news/Schrdinger-to-Present-Preclinical-Data-at-AACR-Annual-Meeting-2025.pdf", "domain": "s203.q4cdn.com", "title": "Schrödinger to Present Preclinical Data at AACR Annual ...", "date": null, "text": "The SGR-4174 presentation will include data characterizing SGR-4174 in preclinical oncology models. ... Preclinical data suggest SGR- 4174 has a di�erentiated pro�le and support its continued development as a potential therapy for patients with KRAS mutant cancers and in rare diseases arising from KRAS pathway mutations."}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://sigma.larvol.com/moa.php?MoaId=705294&tab=newstrac&page=21", "domain": "sigma.larvol.com", "title": "Tumor growth inhib News", "date": "2025-03-25", "text": "SGR-4174 Schrodinger Preclinical characterization of SGR-4174, a potent and selective SOS1 inhibitor for the treatment of pan KRAS mutant cancers in combination with KRAS pathway inhibitors (Section 21; Poster Board No: 11) - Mar 25, 2025 - Abstract #AACR2025AACR_6921; SGR-4174 was well tolerated as monotherapy and in combination with sotorasib or trametinib.SGR-4174 demonstrated favorable PK properties across preclinical species and toxicity profile was well characterized. Our comprehensive preclinical efficacy and safety data support progressing SGR-4174 to clinical development to treat KRAS mutant cancers. ... Similarly, treatment of multiple BRAFV600E patient-derived xenograft (PDX, N=3) models of CRC resulted in synergistic triplet TGI (80%, 102%, 103%) and some tumor regression compared against monotherapy azenosertib (43%, 19%, 51%) or the E + C doublet (49%, 65%, 87%)."}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://altogenlabs.com/xenograft-models/pancreatic-xenograft-models/miapaca-2-xenograft-model/", "domain": "altogenlabs.com", "title": "MIA PaCa-2 Xenograft Model", "date": "2023-03-07", "text": "The MIA PaCa-2 cell line (human pancreas) is used to create the CDX (Cell Line Derived Xenograft) MIA PaCa-2 xenograft mouse model. The MIA PaCa-2 xenograft model exhibits tumor growth inhibition and chemosensitization utilizing monotherapies or in combination (e.g. sulindac, LC-1, parthenolide, gemcitabine)."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/b8e102fe163a4c6eabf652c6ce503310", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "Delving into the Latest Updates on SGR-4174 with Synapse", "date": "2025-04-05", "text": "Clinical Result ... Phase ... Analyzed Enrollment ... Evaluation Publication Date No Data"}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7073299/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "title": "Preclinical assessment with clinical validation of Selinexor ...", "date": "2019-12-12", "text": "Compared to single or dual combination, selinexor-GEM-nab-paclitaxel resulted in almost complete loss of the PDAC spheroids (Figure 2A and 2B). ... Selinexor given at 15 mg/kg every other day x 3weeks caused statistically significant reduction in the growth of PDAC CSC xenograft (Figure 6A and Supplementary Figure 7A, p<0.01). ... Continued shrinkage was seen in each of the subsequent restaging CT scans for at least eight months and was followed by disease stability (Figure 6H)."}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8848, "cached_input_tokens": 5945, "output_tokens": 1780}, "timing": {"search_ms": 473.0, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 18529.8, "total_ms": 19002.8}, "luna_wall_ms": 18529.8, "cost_usd": {"search": 0.001, "jev": 0.0, "luna": 0.0}, "output": {"has_answer": "yes", "summarized_answer": "**AACR 2025** SGR-4174 monotherapy achieved dose-dependent tumor growth inhibition in preclinical pancreatic models [E4][E5]. A review specifies KRAS G12C-mutated xenograft models, including 