{"row_id": "q023", "objective": "Inflammatory Bowel Diseases Mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis Ulcerative Colitis competing agents with the same mechanistic class as Gut Microbiome Dysbiosis, including Live Biotherapeutic Product", "anchors": ["VE202", "MB310", "SER-287", "EXL01"], "facet": "commercial", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 14359, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/blog/drug-asset-due-diligence-report-ser-287-2026-mcp", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "SER-287 Drug Asset Due Diligence Report 2026", "date": "2026-09-11", "text": "*Decision date: 11 September 2026. ... **Phase 2** Highest phase **2** Registered trials **2** Result records **1** Matched deals ## Executive recommendation: CONDITIONAL GO ### Decision memo Advance with milestone-based economics while efficacy durability, safety differentiation, patent scope, and market positioning are validated. The central underwriting question is whether SER-287 can convert its Live biotherapeutic products profile and Not disclosed biology into clinically meaningful differentiation while preserving an investable safety, IP and commercial position. ... |Asset|SER-287 (query alias: SER-287)| |--|--| |Modality / target|Live biotherapeutic products; Not disclosed; Bacteria replacements, Microbiome modulators| |Highest global status|Phase 2| |Originator|Seres Therapeutics, Inc.| |Active developers|Aimmune Therapeutics, Inc.| The MCP disease footprint includes Colitis, Ulcerative. The highest-phase flag is a useful orientation point, but the licensing case depends on indication-level evidence and rights, not the global label alone. ... |NCT03759041|Phase 2|Terminated|203|Primary endpoint not disclosed in English source| |NCT02618187|Phase 1|Completed|58|Primary endpoint not disclosed in English source| ... ### ECO-RESET: A Phase 2B, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled, Multiple Dose, Multicenter Study to Assess Efficacy and Safety of SER-287 in Adults With Active Mild-to-Moderate Ulcerative Colitis **Phase 2**; n=203; evaluation: Not stated in English source. Reported fields: clinical remission = 8 Pts ; clinical remission = 7 Pts ... SER-287 addresses Colitis, Ulcerative. ... The MCP screen returned 1 matched transaction record(s) under the scope “asset-specific.” Partner activity is a market-validation signal, but it does not establish net present value. ... |2016-01-11|Seres Therapeutics Announces Strategic Collaboration with Nestlé Health Science Bowel Disease Therapies in Markets Outside of North America|Not disclosed|US$120.0M upfront; US$1,900.0M stated total| ... ### CONDITIONAL GO Advance with milestone-based economics while efficacy durability, safety differentiation, patent scope, and market positioning are validated. **Required pre-signing gates:** reproduce key efficacy analyses; complete an indication-specific safety review; run a full patent-family and freedom-to-operate search; model risk-adjusted economics by territory; and reconcile all rights, sublicenses and encumbrances."}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://ala.associates/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/240625-Exeliom-MAINTAIN-POP-FR-1.pdf", "domain": "ala.associates", "title": "Exeliom Biosciences collabore avec REMIND sur l’essai", "date": null, "text": " Cette étude de phase 2 vise à évaluer l'efficacité de EXL01 en traitement préventif des récidives post-opératoires chez les patients atteints de la maladie de Crohn ...  La partie A de l'étude MAINTAIN a été arrêtée en raison d’un recrutement trop lent  L'étude MAINTAIN POP commencera début 2025 ; les premiers résultats sont attendus au premier trimestre 2027 Paris, France, le 25 juin 2024 - Exeliom Biosciences, société de biotechnologie au stade clinique développant de nouvelles thérapies en immuno-inflammation et immuno- oncologie, annonce aujourd’hui une collaboration avec REMIND, consortium national de 14 services de gastro-entérologie, autour de MAINTAIN POP, un essai clinique interventionnel post-opératoire de phase 2 dans la maladie de Crohn. Exeliom continue ainsi ses recherches dans la maladie de Crohn après l’arrêt de l’essai clinique MAINTAIN à la fin de la partie A, du fait d’un recrutement trop lent. MAINTAIN POP est un essai de phase 2 randomisé contre placebo auquel participent 13 sites du groupe REMIND. Il vise à recruter 80 patients atteints de la maladie de Crohn et étant entrés en rémission suite à une intervention chirurgicale, afin d'évaluer EXL01 comme traitement d'entretien, seul ou en association avec des anti-TNF. L'étude évaluera la sécurité et l'efficacité de EXL01 par rapport à des critères d'évaluation endoscopiques (par exemple, la récurrence endoscopique six mois après l’intervention). Cette étude interventionnelle post-opératoire est coordonnée par le groupe REMIND. ... L'autorisation pour l'essai clinique MAINTAIN POP sera soumise en septembre 2024, avec pour objectif de commencer le recrutement début 2025 et de publier les principaux résultats au premier trimestre 2027. ... EXL01 est un produit biothérapeutique vivant (LBP - live biotherapeutic product) contenant une souche unique non modifiée de F. prausnitzii, un acteur important du microbiome intestinal humain, qui est développé en tant que nouveau médicament modulant le système immunitaire. ... EXL01 est évalué en clinique dans plusieurs essais cliniques : un essai de phase 1 dans la maladie de Crohn, trois essais de phase 2 en immuno-oncologie en association avec des inhibiteurs de points de contrôle immunitaire et un essai de phase 1/2 dans la prévention à l’infection récurrente à C. difficile."}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/9500af2e0b0346d8b3f9d8d939800b1b", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "Delving into the Latest Updates on EXL-01 with Synapse", "date": "2025-06-18", "text": "Originator Organization Exeliom Biosciences Active Organization Exeliom Biosciences Inactive Organization ... Drug Highest Phase Phase 2 ... CTIS2024-511357-22-00 Recruiting Phase 2 IIT A Phase 2 multicentre, randomised, parallel-arm, placebo-controlled, double-blind study to evaluate the safety and target engagement of EXL01 in the prevention of post-operative recurrence of Crohn’s Disease - REMIND-2024-001 Start Date 31 Mar 2025 ... Phase 2 France Exeliom Biosciences 01 Dec 2024 ... Phase 2 ... 16 Apr 2024 ... Phase 2 France Exeliom Biosciences Crohn Disease Phase 2 France Exeliom Biosciences"}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1609809/000119312521149022/d157894dex991.htm", "domain": "sec.gov", "title": "EX-99.1", "date": null, "text": "*– Topline clinical data from SER-287 Phase 2b study in patients with mild-to-moderate ulcerative * *colitis expected in mid-2021, microbiome biomarker data anticipated in H2 2021 – * ... “Our SER-287 ECO-RESET Phase 2b study in mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis patients is fully enrolled and we anticipate topline clinical results in mid-year. ... **SER-287 Phase 2b ECO-RESET study in ulcerative colitis (UC):** SER-287, an oral microbiome therapeutic candidate consisting of a bacterial consortium, is designed to restructure the gastrointestinal microbiome and reduce inflammation in individuals with UC. Seres has obtained FDA Fast Track designation for SER-287 in active mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis. SER-287 targets restructuring the microbiome to reduce proinflammatory activity and modulate UC-relevant inflammatory pathways, potentially providing a much-needed non-immunosuppressive treatment option to patients suffering from ulcerative colitis. SER-287 has the potential to be used as both a monotherapy and in combination with other approved agents. The SER-287 Phase 2b ECO-RESET study is a randomized, placebo-controlled, three-arm induction trial that has enrolled 203 patients with active mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis who have had inadequate response or loss of response on prior therapy. In arm A, patients receive a short course of vancomycin preconditioning followed by ten weeks of the same daily regimen used in the arm of the Phase 1b trial that showed the highest clinical remission rate. In arm B, patients receive vancomycin preconditioning followed by two weeks of the SER-287 daily regimen as in the first arm, followed by eight weeks of a lower dose of SER-287. In arm C, patients receive placebo. The study’s primary endpoint is the proportion of patients achieving clinical remission at ten weeks. The study will assess endoscopic improvement as a secondary endpoint, as well as a range of microbiome and metabolomic measures. Seres has completed enrollment in the SER-287 Phase 2b ECO-RESET induction study in patients with active mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis and expects to report topline clinical study results in mid-2021, with additional microbiome biomarker data becoming available in H2 2021. ... Seres’ SER-287 program has obtained Fast Track and Orphan Drug designations from the FDA and is being evaluated in a Phase 2b study in patients with active mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis."}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://www.exeliombio.com/news/several-exl01-studies-hit-recruitment-milestones", "domain": "exeliombio.com", "title": "News - exeliom", "date": null, "text": "Inflammatory Disease - Crohn’s Disease - MAINTAIN POP (NCT06925061): Recruitment is ongoing as planned since the launch in April. This is a Phase 2 randomized clinical trial evaluating EXL01 in postoperative Crohn’s disease patients, in collaboration with hashtag#REMIND and 14 French gastroenterology departments. ... - LIVEDIFF (NCT063060): Recruitment has resumed and the first patients have been enrolled in part two of the study."}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://www.exeliombio.com/news/exeliom-biosciences-collaborates-with-remind-in-maintain-pop-study", "domain": "exeliombio.com", "title": "Exeliom Biosciences collaborates with REMIND in MAINTAIN POP ...", "date": null, "text": "· **Phase IItrial will assess efficacy of EXL01 as treatment to prevent post-operative recurrencein patients with Crohn’s disease** ... · **MAINTAIN POP trial to start early 2025 with toplineresults expected in Q1, 2027** **Paris, France, June 25, 2024 –** ExeliomBiosciences, a clinical-stage biotechnology company developing new therapies inimmuno-inflammation and immuno-oncology,today announces its collaboration with REMIND, a nationwide consortium of 14 Frenchgastroenterology departments, in the MAINTAIN POP study, a phase IIpost-operative interventional trial in Crohn’s disease. It will be acontinuation of Exeliom’s efforts in Crohn’s disease after the company decidedto close the MAINTAIN clinical study at the end of Part A due to a slow recruitment. MAINTAIN POP is a phase IIrandomized placebo-controlled trial that will involve 13 sites in the REMINDgroup. It aims to enroll 80 patients with Crohn's disease who have successfullybeen brought to remission by surgery, to evaluate EXL01 as a stand-alonemaintenance treatment or in combination with anti-TNFs. The study will assessboth the safety and efficacy of EXL01 against endoscopic endpoints (e.g.endoscopic recurrence at six months post-surgery). This is a post-operativeinterventional study - coordinated by the REMIND group. MAINTAIN POP is a continuation of thework undertaken in MAINTAIN (NCT05542355), a first-in-human phase I trialevaluating EXL01 for the maintenance of steroid-induced remission in patientswith mild to moderate Crohn’s disease. The preliminary results support agood safety profile for EXL01 in combination with corticosteroids and as amonotherapy in patients with Crohn’s disease, as recently confirmed by theIDMC. ... The clinical trial authorization for MAINTAIN POP willbe submitted in September 2024, with the aim of starting enrollment in early2025 and publishing topline results in Q1, 2027."}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://microbiotica.com/partnering/", "domain": "microbiotica.com", "title": "Partnering - Microbiotica", "date": "2026-05-05", "text": "Microbiotica is collaborating with the Crohn’s & Colitis Foundation for the development of MB310, its Live Biotherapeutic Product, for the treatment of ulcerative colitis (UC). The collaboration has supported the cGMP manufacture of MB310, enabling an Investigational New Drug (IND) application and supporting progression into a first-in-human clinical."}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/985aa1a5aff1423498531f9518d90223", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "SER-287 - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents", "date": null, "text": "|Active Indication Colitis, Ulcerative| ... |License Organization Nestle Health Science SASeres Therapeutics, Inc.| |Drug Highest PhasePhase 2| ... |--|--|--|--|--| |Colitis, Ulcerative|Phase 2|United States|Seres Therapeutics, Inc.|19 Dec 2018| |Colitis, Ulcerative|Phase 2|Canada|Seres Therapeutics, Inc.|19 Dec 2018| ... |NCT03759041 (ECO-RESET, CTgov)|Phase 2|Colitis, Ulcerative|203|Placebo for SER-287 (Placebo (After Placebo Pre-treatment))|zjopgsxadt = xkriqroamm bckpknvwij (uyjdziffpg, wqvnoydebn - qjcbuwcqhx) View more|-|21 Jun 2022| ... |NCT03759041 (ECO-RESET, CTgov)|Phase 2|Colitis, Ulcerative|203|SER-287+Vancomycin Pre-Treatment (SER-287 Induction Dosing (After Vancomycin Pre-treatment))|zjopgsxadt = pjvhacqflt bckpknvwij (uyjdziffpg, mjvnkqkruf - ahxdydjmhw) View more|-|21 Jun 2022|"}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://www.exeliombio.com/news/maintain-pop-submitted-to-ansm", "domain": "exeliombio.com", "title": "MAINTAIN POP submitted to ANSM - Exeliom Biosciences", "date": null, "text": "🔈 We are thrilled to share that the MAINTAIN POP trial was submitted, in collaboration with REMIND, to the ANSM Agence nationale de sécurité du médicament et des produits de santé. MAINTAIN POP is a phase II randomized placebo-controlled trial which will assess the safety and efficacy of EXL01, a single-strain live biotherapeutic, against endoscopic endpoints in patients with Crohn’s disease that have been successfully brought into remission by surgery. The trial will take place across 13 sites in the REMIND group, a network of specialist gastroenterologists in IBD across France."}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/1fb685bb89f84c16af0a3d32e6f4c385", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "VE-202 - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents", "date": null, "text": "|Originator Organization Janssen Research & Development LLC| ... |Active Organization-| |Inactive Organization Vedanta Biosciences, Inc.Janssen Research & Development LLC| |License Organization Janssen Biotech, Inc.Vedanta Biosciences, Inc.| |Drug Highest PhaseDiscontinuedPhase 2| ... |RegulationFast Track (United States)| ... Clinical Trials associated with VE-202 NCT05370885 / TerminatedPhase 2 Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled, Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Patients With Mild-to-Moderate Ulcerative Colitis ... PureTech Founded Entity Vedanta Biosciences Announces Phase 2 Study of VE202 in Ulcerative Colitis Did Not Meet Primary Endpoint ... |--|--|--|--|--| |Colitis, Ulcerative|Phase 2|United States|Vedanta Biosciences, Inc.|12 May 2022|"}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10284, "cached_input_tokens": 6546, "output_tokens": 3088}, "timing": {"search_ms": 533.5, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 34699.2, "total_ms": 35232.7}, "luna_wall_ms": 34699.2, "cost_usd": {"search": 0.001, "jev": 0.0, "luna": 0.0}, "output": {"has_answer": "yes", "summarized_answer": "VE202 (also listed as SER-287, MB310 and EXL01) is associated with microbiome-directed live biotherapeutic profiles in the evidence: SER-287 is an oral bacterial-consortium microbiome therapeutic designed to restructure the gastrointestinal microbiome and reduce inflammation; MB310 is a live biotherapeutic product being developed for ulcerative colitis and progressed into a first-in-human clinical study after cGMP manufacture enabled an IND application; EXL01 is a live biotherapeutic product containing a single, unmodified strain of F. prausnitzii. [E4][E7][E2] VE202 is listed with a Phase 2 mild-to-moderate ulcerative colitis study, NCT05370885, which was terminated and did not meet its primary endpoint; it is also listed with Fast Track status. [E10] SER-287’s ECO-RESET Phase 2b study was randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, multiple-dose and multicenter, enrolled 203 patients, and evaluated clinical remission at ten weeks as its primary endpoint and endoscopic improvement as a secondary endpoint. Its arms used vancomycin preconditioning followed by ten weeks of the same daily regimen, vancomycin preconditioning followed by two weeks of that daily regimen and eight weeks at a lower dose, or placebo. The indexed result record gives clinical remission counts of 8 and 7 patients; the study record lists NCT03759041 as terminated, Phase 2, with 203 participants. [E1][E4][E8] SER-287 also had Fast Track and Orphan Drug designations, and Seres expected topline clinical results in mid-2021 and additional microbiome biomarker data in H2 2021. [E4] MB310’s ulcerative-colitis development status is described as progressing into a first-in-human clinical study. [E7] Seres characterized SER-287 as a potential non-immunosuppressive treatment option for ulcerative colitis. [E4]", "confident_score": 0.62, "missing": "Specific competing agents distinct from the subject, and each competitor’s sponsor, mechanism or class, ulcerative-colitis indication, development stage, trial identifiers, enrollment and results; VE202-specific mechanism or target, route, dose and schedule; detailed VE202 NCT05370885 results and endpoint information; clarification of how the differing profiles listed under the subject’s name forms relate to VE202.", "citations": ["E1", "E2", "E4", "E7", "E8", "E10"], "next_queries": ["VE202 ulcerative colitis competing microbiome agents", "VE202 mechanism target route dose schedule", "VE202 NCT05370885 primary endpoin