{"row_id": "q033", "objective": "DXP-007 sponsor development stage indication public source", "anchors": ["DXP-007"], "facet": null, "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 4111, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://www.zoominfo.com/c/dexpan/4179403", "domain": "zoominfo.com", "title": "Please verify you are a human", "date": null, "text": "Please make sure that Javascript and cookies are enabled on your browser and that you are not blocking them from loading."}, {"id": "E2", "url": "http://www.dxpwind.com/about/dxp-news.html", "domain": "dxpwind.com", "title": "DXP News", "date": null, "text": "Electronic Repair Services ... Click here for the latest DXP news."}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://bcp.dof.ca.gov/2627/FY2627_ORG2740_BCP8680.pdf", "domain": "bcp.dof.ca.gov", "title": "Digital eXperience Platform (DXP) Project", "date": null, "text": "Identification (ID) cards, and Customer Flow Management functions for the public by replacing all obsolete legacy applications and systems."}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://ir.dxpe.com/news/default.aspx", "domain": "ir.dxpe.com", "title": "News", "date": null, "text": "Houston, TX 77040 (713) 996-4700"}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://procureconmro.wbresearch.com/sponsors/2019", "domain": "procureconmro.wbresearch.com", "title": "Sponsors & Exhibitors | ProcureCon MRO 2026", "date": "2026-10-02", "text": "## 2019 Lead Sponsors / Partners ... ### DXP **Website: ** https://www.dxpe.com/ Since 1908, DXP Enterprises, Inc. has been a leading products and service distributor that adds value and total cost savings solutions to industrial customers in virtually every industry. DXP provides innovative pumping solutions, supply chain services and maintenance, repair, operating and production (MROP) products and services. DXP's Supply Chain Services..."}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1020710/000102071020000015/dxpe12311910k.htm", "domain": "sec.gov", "title": "DXP Enterprises, Inc.", "date": null, "text": "**Note:** We do not offer technical support for developing or debugging scripted downloading processes."}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://search.electoralcommission.org.uk/", "domain": "search.electoralcommission.org.uk", "title": "Common searches", "date": null, "text": "The independent body which oversees elections and regulates political finance in the UK This page allows you to search the registers of Political Parties, Non-party campaigners & Referendum Participants, and our database of donations, loans, election/referendum spending & party accounts"}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://logos.fandom.com/wiki/DXP", "domain": "logos.fandom.com", "title": "DXP | Logopedia", "date": "1996-01-01", "text": "In early July 2017, Disney XD announced a new summer program block called **DXP** (stylized as *D|XP*), a program block geared towards gaming and sports."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://status.dxpr.com/", "domain": "status.dxpr.com", "title": "DXPR Status", "date": null, "text": "are necessary for specific functionality on the website. Without them, some features may be disabled."}, {"id": "E10", "url": "http://leg.ufpi.br/subsiteFiles/ppgcf/arquivos/files/Macrophages%20and%20liposomes%20in%20inflammatory%20disease%20Friends%20or%20foes&%2361477;.pdf", "domain": "leg.ufpi.br", "title": "Macrophages and liposomes in inflammatory disease: Friends or foes?", "date": null, "text": "effect of dexamethasone phosphate loaded long-circulating liposomes (LCL-DXP) was evaluated in animal models of multiple sclerosis (MS) and Crohn’s disease (CD). ... a model for MS, treatment ... but not free DXP, resulted ... when compared ... In con- trast, in mice with chronic DSS-induced colitis, a model for CD, treatment with LCL-DXP did not induce an improvement, but in fact worsened the fecal blood loss after treatment, ... CD is a chronic inflammatory dis- ease of the gastrointestinal tract, which together with Colitis Ulcerosa is commonly referred to as inflammatory bowel disease (IBD). ... In the current study, the therapeutic efficacy of liposomal dex- amethasone phosphate (DXP) was assessed in mouse models of MS and CD. DXP is a phosphate derivative of dexamethasone, which is a corticosteroid with strong anti-inflammatory potency. ... from Bipharma Diagnostics B.V. (The Netherlands). ... the ... unexpectedly, ... treatment did not result ... an ... dis- ... In EAE, a model for MS, treatment with liposomal DXP leads to a clinical improvement of the disease, resulting in a reduction of maximal disease intensity and disease ... In contrast, in the DSS- induced colitis model for CD treatment with liposomal DXP leads to a clinical worsening, marked by an increase in fecal blood"}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 5638, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 218}, "timing": {"search_ms": 564.5, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 3235.4, "total_ms": 3799.9}, "luna_wall_ms": 3235.4, "cost_usd": {"search": 0.001, "jev": 0.0, "luna": 0.0}, "output": {"has_answer": "no", "summarized_answer": "", "missing": "DXP-007's sponsor, development stage, indication, and a public source supporting these details.", "citations": [], "next_queries": ["DXP-007 sponsor", "DXP-007 development stage", "DXP-007 indication", "DXP-007 public source"]}, "raw_text": null, "metrics": {"json_valid": true, "has_answer": false, "answer_chars": 0, "confident_score": null, "missing_nothing": false, "missing_empty": false, "n_tags": 0, "invalid_tags": [], "uncited_answer": false, "n_cited_items": 0, "cited_domains": [], "url_in_answer": false, "search_talk": [], "nonempty_when_no": false, "claim_tokens": 0, "ungrounded_tokens": [], "n_ungrounded": 0, "names_subject": false, "subject_in_cited": false, "next_queries": 4, "next_queries_subject_first": 4}}
{"row_id": "q020", "objective": "Inflammatory Bowel Disease competing agents in the same mechanistic class as JTO2, including Monoclonal Antibody and CXCL10 therapies", "anchors": ["JTO2"], "facet": "commercial", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 12970, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/b291dac8a0e24306a1bb17fa4b94e798", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "Delving into the Latest Updates on JT-02(Jyant Technologies) with Synapse", "date": "2025-03-20", "text": "|Drug Type Monoclonal antibody| |--| |Synonyms| |Target CXCL10| |Action antagonists| |Mechanism CXCL10 antagonists(C-X-C motif chemokine ligand 10 antagonists)| |Therapeutic Areas Digestive System Disorders| |Active Indication Inflammatory Bowel Diseases| |Inactive Indication-| |Originator Organization JYANT Technologies, Inc.| ... |Active Organization JYANT Technologies, Inc.| ... |Drug Highest PhasePhase 2| ... |Indication|Highest Phase|Country/Location|Organization|Date| |--|--|--|--|--| |Inflammatory Bowel Diseases|Phase 2|United States|JYANT Technologies, Inc.|30 Jan 2022| ... |Study|Phase|Population|Analyzed Enrollment|Group|Results|Evaluation|Publication Date| |--|--|--|--|--|--|--|--| | | | | | | | | | |--|--|--|--|--|--|--|--| |No Data|No Data|No Data|No Data|No Data|No Data|No Data|No Data| ... Identify the latest clinical trials across global registries."}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6327230/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "title": "Cell Trafficking Interference in Inflammatory Bowel Disease", "date": "2018-08-24", "text": "We discuss the targets that have been explored in clinical trials: chemokines and its receptors (eg, IP10, CCR9), integrins (eg, natalizumab, AJM300, vedolizumab, and etrolizumab), and its endothelial ligands (MAdCAM-1, ICAM-1). ... |CXCL10|CXCR3|Leukocyte recruitment to inflamed intestine.| ... Eldelumab is a fully human monoclonal antibody against Interferon-γ-inducible protein-10 (IP-10). IP-10 or CXCL10 is a chemokine that mediates trafficking of activated T cells, dendritic cells and monocytes to the inflamed colon. Its efficacy was evaluated in both UC (n = 252) and CD (n = 121). In both, eldelumab did not demonstrate efficacy over placebo.^19, 20, 21^ ... These early results are indicative of the efficacy of etrolizumab in treating CD.^47^ Currently, phase 3 clinical trials are ongoing in CD and UC, evaluating etrolizumab safety and efficacy. An ongoing clinical trial in UC will compare the effectiveness of etrolizumab with anti-TNF.^48, 49, 50, 51^ ... PTG-100 (Protagonist) is a novel oral α4β7 antagonist peptide with minimal systemic absorption and distribution largely restricted to the gut. PTG-100 was evaluated in patients with moderate to severe ulcerative colitis in the phase 2b PROPEL study and was discontinued because it did not meet its primary endpoint of clinical remission.^53, 54^ ... MAdCAM-1 Blockade (PF-00547659/SHP647) is a humanized monoclonal antibody against MAdCAM-1 (the endothelial ligand for integrin α4β7). Recently, the results of the TURANDOT—a phase 2, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial in patients with UC—have been reported. ... ^65^ The Opera II was a 72-week, phase 2 extension study designed to assess the long safety and efficacy of SHP647 (Shire designation). A total of 268 patients were enrolled, and 149 completed the study. ... ClinicalTrial.gov. NCT00457171 GI-270384 Study In Patients With Mild To Moderate Ulcerative Colitis. https://clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/NCT00457171? term=selectin&cond=ulcerative+colitis&rank=1."}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/gastroenterology/articles/10.3389/fgstr.2026.1747118/full", "domain": "frontiersin.org", "title": "Advancing therapeutic frontiers: a pipeline of novel drugs ...", "date": "2026-01-30", "text": "|IP-10 antagonist|Eldelumab (BMS-936557)|Fully human monoclonal IgG1 antibody targeting IP-10/CXCL10|NCT00656890, NCT01294410|Phase 2, Phase 2b|Completed; failed to meet primary endpoints| ... |CCL11 antagonist|Bertilimumab|Recombinant human IgG4 monoclonal antibody neutralizing eotaxin-1|NCT01671956|Phase 2|Status unknown as of Jan 2018; remained as recruiting| ... Abrilumab, a human monoclonal IgG2 antibody targeting α4β7 integrin, was evaluated in two Phase 2 studies for moderate-to-severe UC. ... Leiolizumab is a tetravalent agonist IgG1 antibody targeting PSGL-1 being evaluated in a Phase 2a, multicenter, single-arm, open-label study (NCT06109441) for moderately to severely active UC refractory to biologic therapy. ... Bertilimumab is a recombinant human IgG4 monoclonal antibody that neutralizes human eotaxin-1 (CCL11), a chemokine involved in eosinophil recruitment and activation. ... CU104 is a new oral investigational drug that specifically inhibits IL1β, IL-6, and TNFα (69). It is being studied in a double-blind, placebo-controlled, multi-center Phase 2 RCT (NCT05907330) designed to evaluate its efficacy and safety in patients with moderate to severe UC."}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8129496/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "title": "Targeting Immune Cell Trafficking – Insights From Research Models ...", "date": "2021-05-04", "text": "Treatment with anti-CXCL10 antibodies attenuated colitis in IL10-deficient mice and in DSS colitis and reduced cell infiltration to the lamina propria (73–76). In clinical studies, treatment with a monoclonal antibody against CXCL10 was efficient for the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis (MDX-1100) (77). However, blocking CXCL10 with the antibody eldelumab failed to induce remission in patients with moderate-to-severe UC or CD (78–80). Still, in subgroups of anti-TNFα naïve patients, CXCL10 blockade ameliorated mucosal response, suggesting that this treatment could be effective in selected patients (66). ... However, to our knowledge, no CCL20 antagonist has been used in clinical trials of IBD so far. ... Aiming to expand the clinically successful anti-α4β7 strategy, the humanized monoclonal antibody etrolizumab was developed to target the β7-subunit of α4β7 as well as αE (CD103) β7 integrin hetereodimers (110). ... |CXCL10|Epithelium|Eldelumab|Monoclonal antibody|IL-10^-/-^ and piroxicam colitis mouse model (74)|Yes|UC (Phase II) (78)|IV|No|Improvement of IBDQ score| |CXCL10|Epithelium|Eldelumab|Monoclonal antibody|DSS colitis mouse model (75)|Yes|UC (Phase II) (80)|IV|No|N/A| |CXCL10|Epithelium|Eldelumab|Monoclonal antibody|IL-10^-/-^ colitis mouse model (76)|Yes|CD (Phase II) (79)|IV|No|Numerically higher remission and response rates|"}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lanrhe/article/PIIS2665-9913(23)00274-6/fulltext", "domain": "thelancet.com", "title": "Cloudflare", "date": null, "text": "Cloudflare is currently unable to resolve your requested domain (www.thelancet.com). There are two potential causes of this:"}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://jyanttech.com/index.php?/pipeline", "domain": "jyanttech.com", "title": "Product Pipeline Summary", "date": null, "text": "|Product (Target)|Indication|Pre-Clin.|Phase 1|Phase 2|Phase 3| |--|--|--|--|--|--| |JT02 (CXCL10)|IBD| |JT03 (CXCL13)|RA, Solid Tumors| |JT04 (CCL25)|Solid Tumors| |JT05 (CXCL16)|Solid Tumors| |JT06 (CXCL11)|MS| |JT07 (CXCR3 CXCR7)|IBD, Solid Tumors| |JT08 (CXCR5)|Solid Tumors| |Nanocisplatin|Solid Tumors| |Nanoflavopiridol|HRPC| |Nanocurcumin|RA, Solid Tumors| |Nanoresveratrol|Solid Tumors| Diagnostic Product Pipeline (coming soon)"}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://www.dovepress.com/optimising-monoclonal-antibody-drug-development-for-inflammatory-bowel-peer-reviewed-fulltext-article-CEG", "domain": "dovepress.com", "title": "Optimising Monoclonal Antibody Therapies for Inflammatory Bowel ...", "date": "2025-09-30", "text": "**Abstract:** Despite the success of monoclonal antibody (mAb) therapies in treating inflammatory bowel disease (IBD), a persistent therapeutic ceiling remains. This comprehensive review explores emerging strategies to enhance the efficacy of mAb-based treatments. Key among these is the development of bispecific antibodies designed to simultaneously engage two cytokine targets, offering dual blockade of inflammatory pathways and the potential for synergistic effects. Co-formulation approaches, comprising two or more mAbs within a single therapeutic product, are also examined as a means of broadening immunologic coverage and streamlining delivery. Finally, advances in pharmacokinetic optimisation are discussed, including Fc region modifications, polyethylene glycol conjugation, albumin fusion, and glycoengineering, all aimed at reducing immunogenicity and extending half-life. ... ### Modifying the Fc Region ... ^22,23^ There are no current afucosylated mAbs licenced for IBD or immune mediated inflammatory disorders (IMIDs) but given the feasibility of the technology and the demonstrated impact upon NK cells via enhanced ADCC activity, it remains an area of interest. ... All three of vedolizumab, mirikizumab and risankizumab are licenced for IBD and contain such Fc modifications and demonstrate the plausibility of this technology for real-world practice.^65^ There are several other types of mutations or modifications, such as the STR mutation in the CH2 domain of the Fc, that offer promise in Fc engineering of mAbs to reduce immunogenic potential.^65^ ... Several bsAbs targeting various cytokines are currently in development (Table 2). ... Two novel bsAbs targeting TNFα and IL-23 are currently in development, with Phase 2 trials anticipated.^102,103^ ... Further bsAbs targeting TL1A are in the pipeline. HXN1002 targets both TL1A and α4β7 integrin, which mediates the homing of lymphocytes to gut-associated lymphoid tissue via binding to MAdCAM-1 on endothelial cells.^110^ Preclinical studies presented by SPYRE Therapeutics in 2025 showed enhanced efficacy of dual inhibition in murine colitis models, and a Phase 2 study evaluating the extended half-life antibodies as single agents and pairwise combinations that started in 2025.^111^"}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://clinicaltrials.ucsf.edu/inflammatory-bowel-disease", "domain": "clinicaltrials.ucsf.edu", "title": "UCSF Inflammatory Bowel Disease Clinical Trials for 2026 ...", "date": "2026-09-24", "text": "# Inflammatory Bowel Disease clinical trials at UCSF 27 in progress, 11 open to eligible people ... All ages Under 18 Over 18 - ## Adverse Events, Change in Disease Activity, and How Intravenous and Subcutaneous Risankizumab Moves Through the Body of Pediatric Participants With Moderately to Severely Active Crohn's Disease open to eligible people ages 2-17 ... This study will assess the pharmacokinetics, efficacy, and safety of risankizumab in pediatric participants with moderately to severely active CD aged 2 to < 18 years old who have had intolerance or inadequate response to other therapies. ... The CAMEO study has been started to help understand what factors are important in determining whether a child with CD completely heals the inflammation after anti-TNF therapy. The investigators will do that by measuring certain markers of inflammation in the blood and stool and by looking at a person's genes (DNA) and how inflammation is controlled in the intestine. ... This study will assess how safe and effective oral Upadacitinib is in treating moderately to severely active Crohn's Disease in pediatric participants aged 2 to 18 years old who have had inadequate response, loss of response, intolerance, or medical contraindications to corticosteroids, immunosuppressants, and/or biologic therapy. ... The purpose of this study is to determine the safety, efficacy, and pharmacokinetics (PK) of etrasimod for the treatment of moderately to severely active ulcerative colitis in adolescents (≥ 12 years up to < 18 years of age). ... This research study is testing an investigational research product called TRX103 as a possible treatment for individuals suffering from Crohn's Disease (CD). The primary purpose of this study is to learn how safe and effective different doses of TRX103 are when administered to individuals with CD. ... A multicenter study to evaluate the efficacy and safety of maintenance and long-term treatment administration of upadacitinib, an orally administered Janus kinase 1 inhibitor, in adult participants with Crohn's Disease."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://jillrobertsibdcenter.weillcornell.org/research-and-clinical-trials/clinical-trials", "domain": "jillrobertsibdcenter.weillcornell.org", "title": "Clinical Trials | Jill Roberts Center for Inflammatory Bowel ...", "date": null, "text": "The Jill Roberts Center for Inflammatory Bowel Disease (JRC) has an active clinical trials and translational research program. See below for a list of actively recruiting clinical trials and translational research trials. Patients who are interested in participating in a clinical trial should contact Fatiha Chabouni at (212) 746-5109."}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ueg2.12305", "domain": "onlinelibrary.wiley.com", "title": "Landscape of new drugs and targets in inflammatory bowel disease", "date": "2022-12-01", "text": "lthough UST (an inhibitor of p40 subunit) has been shown to be effective in IBD,^8^ the p19 antagonists (selective IL-23 inhibitors) have proven to be more effective than UST in other immune-mediated conditions, leading us to evaluate them in IBD.^15, 16^ Four IL-23 p19 inhibitors are currently being evaluated in IBD: risankizumab, guselkumab, brazikumab and mirikizumab."}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10025, "cached_input_tokens": 6546, "output_tokens": 4085}, "timing": {"search_ms": 811.8, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 43046.8, "total_ms": 43858.6}, "luna_wall_ms": 43046.8, "cost_usd": {"search": 0.001, "jev": 0.0, "luna": 0.0}, "output": {"has_answer": "yes", "summarized_answer": "JTO2 (JT-02) is a CXCL10 antagonist monoclonal antibody for inflammatory bowel diseases, listed at Phase 2 in the United States with a date of 30 January 2022. [E1] JYANT Technologies’ pipeline also lists JT07, targeting CXCR3 and CXCR7 for IBD. [E6] Eldelumab (BMS-936557) is a fully human IgG1 monoclonal antibody targeting IP-10/CXCL10; it completed Phase 2 and Phase 2b studies (NCT00656890 and NCT01294410) and failed to meet primary endpoints. [E3] Its efficacy was evaluated in ulcerative colitis (252 participants) and Crohn’s disease (121 participants), without efficacy over placebo; a review also reports failure to induce remission in moderate-to-severe UC or CD, while noting improved mucosal response in subgroups of anti-TNFα-naïve patients. [E2][E4] A review table lists IV administration and an improvement in IBDQ score for a Phase II UC study, no improvement for another Phase II UC study, and numerically higher remission and response rates in a Phase II CD study. [E4] MDX-1100 is another monoclonal antibody studied against CXCL10, with treatment efficacy stated for rheumatoid arthritis. [E4]\n\nOther named IBD agents in the evidence include etrolizumab, a β7-subunit-targeting antibody, with Phase 3 trials ongoing in CD and UC and a UC trial comparing it with anti-TNF; early results were described as indicative of efficacy in CD. [E2][E4] PTG-100 is an oral α4β7 antagonist peptide evaluated in the Phase 2b PROPEL study in moderate-to-severe UC; it was discontinued after missing its primary endpoint of clinical remission. [E2] PF-00547659/SHP647 is a humanized monoclonal antibody against MAdCAM-1; TURANDOT was a Phase 2 randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled UC trial, and the 72-week Phase 2 Opera II extension enrolled 268 patients, of whom 149 completed the study. [E2] The IBD review also names natalizumab, AJM300 and vedolizumab among integrin agents explored in clinical trials. [E2] Bertilimumab is a recombinant human IgG4 antibody neutralizing CCL11/eotaxin-1, listed with NCT01671956 at Phase 2; its status was described as unknown as of January 2018 and as remaining recruiting. [E3] Abrilumab is a human IgG2 antibody targeting α4β7, evaluated in two Phase 2 studies for moderate-to-severe UC. [E3] Leiolizumab is a tetravalent agonist IgG1 antibody targeting PSGL-1, evaluated in a Phase 2a multicenter, single-arm, open-label study (NCT06109441) in moderately-to-severely active UC refractory to biologic therapy. [E3] CU104 inhibits IL1β, IL-6 and TNFα and is being studied in a double-blind, placebo-controlled, multicenter Phase 2 RCT (NCT05907330) in moderate-to-severe UC. [E3] The evidence also names risankizumab, guselkumab, brazikumab and mirikizumab as IL-23 p19 inhibitors being evaluated in IBD. [E10] HXN1002 targets TL1A and α4β7; preclinical studies in murine colitis models were presented in 2025, and a Phase 2 study of extended-half-life antibodies as single agents and pairwise combinations started in 2025. [E7]", "confident_score": 0.78, "missing": "For JTO2, the route, dose and schedule; trial name and registry ID; enrollment and eligibility; regulatory designations; and clinical results are not stated. For JT07, the development stage, trial details and results are not stated. For MDX-1100, an IBD indication, development stage and IBD trial results are not stated. For etrolizumab, PTG-100, PF-00547659/SHP647, natalizumab, AJM300, vedolizumab, bertilimumab, abrilumab, leiolizumab, CU104, risankizumab, guselkumab, brazikumab, mirikizumab and HXN1002, details not supplied for each agent include any omitted trial enrollment, eligibility, dose or route, and efficacy results. Direct comparative results between JTO2 and the named agents are not stated.", "citations": ["E1", "E2", "E3", "E4", "E6", "E7", "E10"], "next_queries": ["JTO2 JT-02 trial registry enrollment eligibility", "JTO2 JT-02 route dose schedule", "JTO2 JT-02 clinical results CXCL10", "JTO2 JT-02 regulatory designations", "JTO2 JT-02 comparative efficacy IBD"]}, "raw_text": null, "metrics": {"json_valid": true, "has_answer": true, "answer_chars": 2983, "confident_score": 0.78, "missing_nothing": false, "missing_empty": false, "n_tags": 18, "invalid_tags": [], "uncited_answer": false, "n_cited_items": 7, "cited_domains": ["dovepress.com", "frontiersin.org", "jyanttech.com", "onlinelibrary.wiley.com", "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "synapse.patsnap.com"], "url_in_answer": false, "search_talk": [], "nonempty_when_no": false, "claim_tokens": 72, "ungrounded_tokens": ["JTO2", "January", "Phase II UC", "Phase II CD", "The IBD"], "n_ungrounded": 5, "names_subject": true, "subject_in_cited": false, "next_queries": 5, "next_queries_subject_first": 5}}
{"row_id": "q035", "objective": "BS-HH-002 first regulatory approval or market launch year in acute myeloid leukemia", "anchors": ["BS-HH-002"], "facet": "catalysts", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 13997, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://patents.google.com/patent/EP2765133A1/en", "domain": "patents.google.com", "title": "Acylated derivative of homoharringtonine, preparation method therefor, and application thereof", "date": "2012-08-20", "text": "- HHT can be applied in the remission induction and post-remission treatment of acute myeloid leukemia, in the treatment of myelodysplastic syndrome (MDS), chronic myelogenous leukemia, polycythemia vera and malignant lymphoma, etc., particularly in the treatment of acute non-lymphocytic leukemia ... - BS-HH-002 improves the anti-Kasumi-1 (acute myeloid leukemia M2 type, AML-M2) activity by more than 3.4-fold, improves the anti-K562/adr (drug-resistant, chronic myeloid leukemia, CML) activity by more than 3.2-fold, improves the anti-NB4 (acute promyelocytic leukemia, AML) activity by more than 3-fold, and improves the anti-H9 (acute lymphoblastic leukemia, ALL) activities by more than 5-fold. ... - BS-HH-002 has an inhibition rate of over 40% of transplanted tumor of leukemia under the dosage of both 0.1 and 0.3mg/kg. ... Clinical studies demonstrate that HHT can be applied in the remission induction and post-remission treatment of acute myeloid leukemia, in the treatment of myelodysplastic syndrome (MDS), chronic myelogenous leukemia, polycythemia vera and malignant lymphoma, etc., particularly in the treatment of acute non-lymphocytic leukemia [ZHANG, Zhixue et al., Clinical study of HAG projects for the treatment of middle and high risk myeloid hyperplasia singular syndrome and acute myeloid leukemia, Journal of Jinggangshan University, 2010, 31(6),108-110;"}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/e8d3b9c25ec941369c758ac88507fd6c", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "Delving into the Latest Updates on BS-HH-002 with Synapse", "date": "2025-05-22", "text": "Active Indication Acute Myeloid Leukemia ... License Organization Drug Highest Phase Phase 1 First Approval Date ... A Phase I, Open-Label, Dose Escalation and Cohort Expansion Study of BS HH 002.SA in Patients With Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) and Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) Indication:Relapsed or refractory AML in patients for whom no established treatment options are available (this indication will heretofore be referred to as the protocol AML indication), or adult patients with MDS who are classified as high risk or very high risk according to the Revised International Prognosis Scoring System (IPSS-R)."}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8633684/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "title": "Therapeutic effects of an innovative BS-HH-002 drug on ...", "date": "2021-11-27", "text": "BS-HH-002 is a newly developed drug with excellent antitumor activity, which resulted from the modification and optimization of the side structure of the homoharringtonine (HHT). It is particularly efficient in treatment for acute myeloid leukemia and myelodysplastic syndromes. ... BS-HH-002 has been well validated for treatment of AML and MDS. The drug has been approved by the FDA to enter a phase 1 clinical study in 2018."}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://exaly.com/paper-pdf/76406053/citation-report.pdf", "domain": "exaly.com", "title": "[PDF] MCL-1 inhibitors, fast-lane development of a new class of anti-canc ...", "date": null, "text": "Therapeutic effects of an innovative BS-HH-002 drug on pancreatic cancer cells via induction of complete MCL-1 degradation."}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11821653/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "title": "Homoharringtonine: mechanisms, clinical applications and ...", "date": "2025-01-30", "text": "In 2012, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approved HHT (omacetaxine mepesuccinate) for treating chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) (13). ... HHT has demonstrated significant efficacy in the treatment of hematological malignancies, particularly in AML and CML. Currently, the clinical application of HHT is under investigation, including its potential as a monotherapy and in combination with other medications. HHT has demonstrated significant efficacy in the treatment of AML. A Phase II clinical trial involving 46 patients with refractory and/or relapsed (R/R) AML indicated that 80% of the patients achieved complete remission (151). Despite all patients experiencing severe neutropenia and thrombocytopenia during induction therapy, the therapeutic efficacy of HHT remains noteworthy. Another Phase II clinical trial assessed the efficacy of the combination of sorafenib and HHT in patients with Fms-like tyrosine kinase 3-internal tandem duplication (FLT3-ITD) positive AML (152). Among the 24 patients, 20 of 24 patients (83.3%) achieved complete remission (true or with inadequate hematologic recovery). In addition, in a multicenter Phase II trial, the regimen combining venetoclax, cytarabine, and HHT was found to be promising and well-tolerated for the treatment of R/R AML (153). ... |7|AML|Sorafenib and omacetaxine mepesuccinate as a safe and effective treatment for acute myeloid leukemia carrying internal tandem duplication of Fms-like tyrosine kinase 3|PhaseII|CR/CRi: Among R/R patients, 28 achieved CR or CRi. Among newly diagnosed patients, 4 achieved CR and 1 achieved CRi.LFS: Median LFS was 5.6 months.OS: Median OS was 10.9 months.|(164)| ... |9|AML|Optimization of idarubicin and cytarabine induction regimen with homoharringtonine for newly diagnosed acute myeloid leukemia patients based on the peripheral blast clearance rate: A single-arm, phase 2 trial (RJ-AML 2014)|Phase II|CR rate: 84.4% overall, with 87.5% in D5-PBCR (–) group and 80.0% in D5-PBCR (+) group.mOS: Not reached in the entire cohort.mEFS: 42.2 months.|(166)| ... Additionally, semi-synthetic homoharringtonine (ssHHT) demonstrates favorable pharmacokinetics and low inter-patient variability in patients with advanced AML (215). Furthermore, BS-HH-002, a novel HHT derivative, has demonstrated significantly enhanced anti-tumor activity through structural optimization. Specifically, in the treatment of pancreatic cancer, it effectively inhibits cell proliferation and induces apoptosis by degrading the anti-apoptotic protein MCL-1."}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://med.agiltrace.com/clinical-trials/NCT04743115", "domain": "med.agiltrace.com", "title": "A Phase I, Open-Label, Dose Escalation and Cohort Expansion Study of BS HH 002.SA in Patients With AML and MDS", "date": null, "text": "Indication:Relapsed or refractory AML in patients for whom no established treatment options are available (this indication will heretofore be referred to as the protocol AML indication), or adult patients with MDS who are classified as high risk or very high risk according to the Revised International Prognosis Scoring System (IPSS-R). Number of Investigators and Study Centers:Up to 5 Investigators in the US. Objectives:Dose Escalation Part Primary Objective: 1. To determine the maximum tolerated dose (MTD) of BS HH 002.SA administered subcutaneously once per day for 12 days of a 28-day cycle. Secondary Objectives: 2. To provide an initial safety profile of single and multiple cycles of BS HH 002.SA. 3. To assess the pharmacokinetic (PK) profile of BS HH 002.SA. 4. To explore the anti-tumor activity of BS HH 002.SA in patients with the protocol AML indication or high-risk MDS. ... Primary Objectives: 1. To evaluate safety and tolerability of BS HH 002.SA at MTD and/or lower dose level (DL) in selected cohorts of patients with the protocol AML indication or high-risk MDS. 2. To evaluate preliminary anti-tumor activity of BS HH 002.SA at MTD and/or lower DL in selected cohorts of patients with the protocol AML indication or high-risk MDS. ... Study Population:Adult patients with the protocol AML indication or high-risk MDS. ## Conditions - Acute Myeloid Leukemia, Myelodysplastic Syndrome ... - **DRUG** BS HH 002.SA The Dose Escalation Part is a 3+3 design dose escalation study to determine the MTD of BS HH 002.SA in up to approximately 30 patients with the protocol AML indication or high risk MDS. Cohorts of 3 patients will be sequentially assigned to receive BS HH 002.SA at escalating DLs following the standard 3+3 dose escalation design, with 3 to 6 patients at each DL. Cohort Expansion Part: Following determination of the MTD, the study will continue at the MTD and/or a lower DL ## Sponsors & Collaborators - Shanghai Bensen Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd. lead INDUSTRY ... ## Timeline & Regulatory - **Start** 2021-02-28 - **Primary Completion** 2025-02-28 - **Completion** 2025-02-28 - **FDA Drug** Yes"}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://patents.google.com/patent/WO2013023622A1/zh", "domain": "patents.google.com", "title": "高三尖杉酯碱的酰化衍生物、及其制备方法和应用", "date": "2012-08-20", "text": "- BS-HH-002 6-acetyl homoharringtonine."}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://aacrjournals.org/cancerres/article/77/13_Supplement/4068/619655/Abstract-4068-HH-002-a-derivative-of", "domain": "aacrjournals.org", "title": "Abstract 4068: HH-002, a derivative of Homoharringtonine, show promsing in diverse cancer models in preclinical characterization", "date": "2017-07-01", "text": "Homoharringtonine (HHT) is an anti-cancer drug used to treat imatinib resistant CML, and a reversible inhibitor of translation acting upon the early steps in polypeptide chain elongation. BS-HH-002.SA is a derivative of HHT. BS-HH-002. SA was shown to decrease the phosphorylation of Janus protein tyrosine kinase 2 (JAK2) as well as downstream targets, such as signal transducers and activators of transcription 3 and 5 (STAT3 and STAT 5), it also reduced Myeloid cell leukemia-1 (Mcl-1) protein level significantly and resulted in apoptosis. ... Efficacy of BS-HH-002 was tested in a recombinant human erythropoietin injection (rhEpo)-induced murine model of polycythemia Vera, Treatment with BS-HH-002. SA BID for 4 days showed a significant inhibitory effect on rhEpo induced increase in reticulocytes, hematocrit and splenomegaly, as well as in red blood cell, white blood cell and platelet counts. Furthermore, histology evaluations revealed that BS-HH-002.SA exerted an inhibitory effect on rhEpo induced extramedullary hematopoiesis in spleen, and decreased cellularity in bone marrow with more predominant effect on erythroid cells than on myeloid cells."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://www.withpower.com/trial/bsb-1001-for-blood-cancers-8a66b", "domain": "withpower.com", "title": "BSB-1001 for Blood Cancers - Clinical Trials", "date": "2024-07-03", "text": "BSB-1001 for Blood Cancers · Info for Participants · Phase Phase 1 & 2 Clinical Trial 2026 | Power | Power ... This trial is no longer recruiting.My employer runs this trial ... No longer recruiting at 7 trial locations ... Trial Phase: Phase 1 & 2 Sponsor: BlueSphere Bio, Inc ... This trial tests a new cellular therapy called BSB-1001 for certain blood cancers, such as AML, ALL, and MDS. Researchers aim to determine if BSB-1001 is safe and effective in preventing cancer recurrence. ... Participants must have a matched donor for the treatment. As a Phase 1 trial, participants will be among the first to receive this new treatment, aiding researchers in understanding its effects in people. ... Although BSB-1001 remains in the early testing stages, similar treatments are usually well-tolerated. This trial is in its early phases, meaning researchers are beginning to gather safety information, but a complete safety profile is not yet available. ... In this trial, participants will receive BSB-1001 in different treatment arms, including dose escalation cohorts and an expansion dose cohort. ... This trial is for patients with blood cancers like AML, ALL, or MDS who are getting a stem cell transplant from a donor that matches their tissue type. Participants should not have had previous treatments that would interfere with the study. ... I have a high-risk blood cancer such as AML, ALL, or MDS. Suitable for one of the approved conditioning regimens as defined in the protocol ... The study tests BSB-1001, an experimental cellular therapy added to standard care (SOC), in two parts: first, finding the right dose and then seeing how well it works at preventing cancer relapse after stem cell transplants. ... AML, ALL and MDS HLA-A\\*02:01 and HA-1-positive (H/H or H/R) patients with an identified HLA-matched, HA-1-negative (R/R) donor will be dosed in dose escalation cohorts ... Once the maximum tolerated dose (MTD) or promising dose is reached additional AML HLA-A\\*02:01 and HA-1-positive (H/H or H/R) patients with an identified HLA-matched, HA-1-negative (R/R) donor will be enrolled in the expansion cohort. ... BlueSphere Bio, Inc ... BS-HH-002, a modified version of homoharringtonine, shows strong antitumor activity against pancreatic cancer by completely degrading the anti-apoptosis protein MCL-1, leading to inhibited cell growth and increased cell death. In animal studies, BS-HH-002 demonstrated a faster absorption into the bloodstream and significantly less heart toxicity compared to its predecessor, HHT, suggesting it may be a safer and more effective treatment option for solid tumors. ... The goal of this clinical trial is to test BSB-1001 which is a new type of cellular therapy to treat blood cancers (AML, ALL and MDS). ... BSB-1001 is a highly potent cell therapy with the potential to be an effective in treatment for patients with AML undergoing alloSCT. ... BSB-1001 is an engineered TCR T cell therapy that targets the blood-restricted antigen, HA-1."}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/organization/4b3d5fc1a7fe700ca8fe9b70c3c6ae59", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "Delving into the Latest Updates on Shanghai Bensen Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd. with Synapse", "date": "2025-07-30", "text": "Phase 1 A Phase I, Open-Label, Dose Escalation and Cohort Expansion Study of BS HH 002.SA in Patients With Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) and Myelodysplastic Syndrome (MDS) Indication:Relapsed or refractory AML in patients for whom no established treatment options are available (this indication will heretofore be referred to as the protocol AML indication), or adult patients with MDS who are classified as high risk or very high risk according to the Revised International Prognosis Scoring System (IPSS-R). ... BS-HH-002 ( Mcl-1 ) Acute Myeloid Leukemia"}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 9153, "cached_input_tokens": 5547, "output_tokens": 278}, "timing": {"search_ms": 529.8, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 4332.8, "total_ms": 4862.6}, "luna_wall_ms": 4332.8, "cost_usd": {"search": 0.001, "jev": 0.0, "luna": 0.0}, "output": {"has_answer": "no", "summarized_answer": "", "missing": "BS-HH-002's first regulatory approval year or market launch year in acute myeloid leukemia.", "citations": [], "next_queries": ["BS-HH-002 acute myeloid leukemia regulatory approval year", "BS-HH-002 acute myeloid leukemia market launch year"]}, "raw_text": null, "metrics": {"json_valid": true, "has_answer": false, "answer_chars": 0, "confident_score": null, "missing_nothing": false, "missing_empty": false, "n_tags": 0, "invalid_tags": [], "uncited_answer": false, "n_cited_items": 0, "cited_domains": [], "url_in_answer": false, "search_talk": [], "nonempty_when_no": false, "claim_tokens": 0, "ungrounded_tokens": [], "n_ungrounded": 0, "names_subject": false, "subject_in_cited": false, "next_queries": 2, "next_queries_subject_first": 2}}
