{"row_id": "q029", "objective": "TP-317 in vivo monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression tumour shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma animal models", "anchors": ["TP-317 KPC", "TP-317"], "facet": "readout", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 7517, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://aacrjournals.org/cancerres/article/83/7_Supplement/1135/722183/Abstract-1135-TP317-a-first-in-class-resolvin-E1", "domain": "aacrjournals.org", "title": "Abstract 1135: TP317, a first-in-class resolvin E1 small molecule, potentiates the efficacy of immune checkpoint (ICI) inhibitors in ICI-resistant and ICI-sensitive tumors", "date": null, "text": "Methods: Subcutaneous murine models of lung (LLC), melanoma (B16F10), and pancreatic (Panc02; KPC) tumors were used to investigate TP-317 monotherapy and combinations with ICI. ... In KRAS-mutant KPC tumors (N=10/group), TP317 (7.5 µg Q6D) demonstrated significant anti-tumor activity compared to placebo (500 ± 110 vs 1314 ± 106 mm 3; p<0.001) and was comparable to anti-PD1, while TP-317 + anti-PD1 was superior to anti-PD1 alone (353 ± 82 vs 710 ± 106 mm 3; p<0.01). In Panc02 and KPC models, TP317’s anti-tumor efficacy was attenuated by CD8+ T cell or NK cell depletion. ... Conclusions: TP317 monotherapy and ICI combinations significantly inhibited tumor growth in various murine models of cancer. ... In summary, TP317, an RvE1 drug with a high therapeutic index, has potent single agent efficacy and offers a novel approach in combination with ICI to treat ICI-resistant and ICI-sensitive tumors."}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://www.kmcc.nhs.uk/s3/assets/lun-043-pembrolizumab,-carboplatin-and-paclitaxel-v4.pdf", "domain": "kmcc.nhs.uk", "title": "Pembrolizumab, carboplatin and paclitaxel 1 of 5", "date": null, "text": "Maximum of 4 cycles of pembrolizumab, carboplatin & paclitaxel followed by, in the absence of disease progression, continued treatment with pembrolizumab monotherapy* to continue for a total treatment duration of 2 years (maximum of 35 cycles including the initial 4 induction cycles of treatment or its equivalent if 6-weekly pembrolizumab monotherapy dosing is used from cycle 5) or until disease progression or unacceptable toxicity or withdrawal of patient consent, whichever occurs first. *There are 2 alternative dosing schedules for pembrolizumab monotherapy, 200mg IV every 3 weeks or 400mg IV every 6 weeks. ... Cycle 5 onwards: Repeat every 21 days"}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://www.cell.com/molecular-therapy-family/oncology/fulltext/S2372-7705(22)00151-6", "domain": "cell.com", "title": "Cloudflare", "date": null, "text": "Please try again in a few minutes. ... If you are using a CNAME origin record, make sure it is valid and resolvable."}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://openurl.ebsco.com/contentitem/doi:10.7150/thno.56737?id=ebsco:doi:10.7150/thno.56737", "domain": "openurl.ebsco.com", "title": "Detail - OpenURL Connection", "date": "2025-05-30", "text": "We were unable to find your item with the information provided. \"Access through your institution\" to search for it on your institution's EBSCOhost experience."}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://www.sbir.gov/awards/203006", "domain": "sbir.gov", "title": "Award | SBIR", "date": null, "text": "To address this opportunity, Thetis is developing TP-317, a Resolvin E1 (RvE1) therapy for PC. ... Preliminary research conducted in collaboration with Dr. Dipak Panigrahy’s Lab (Harvard Medical School) has shown that TP-317 can suppress tumor growth in multiple animal models as a single agent and has an additive effect with chemotherapy. ... The overall goal of this Fast Track grant is to complete key preclinical studies to support an investigational new drug (IND) application and advance TP-317 into clinical trials for the treatment of PC. ... Phase I, Specific Aim 1: To investigate TP-317 in Murine Pancreatic Cancer Models. The efficacy of TP- 317 will be assessed in two established mouse models of PC, the KPC model and a patient derived xenograft model. ... Phase I Milestones: Improvement in survival and tumor volume greater than 25% with TP-317 monotherapy or combination arm compared to placebo or active comparator and identification of biomarkers that correlate with response/non-response preclinically, are clinically significant in PC and are easily assayed in clinical trials. Phase II, Specific Aim 2. ... Phase II, Specific Aim 3."}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://cdn.clinicaltrials.gov/large-docs/61/NCT05508061/SAP_001.pdf", "domain": "cdn.clinicaltrials.gov", "title": "���������", "date": null, "text": "� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������"}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://www.sbir.gov/portfolio/406944", "domain": "sbir.gov", "title": "Firm | SBIR", "date": null, "text": "The efficacy of TP- 317 will be assessed in two established mouse models of PC, the KPC model and a patient derived xenograft model. ... Phase I Milestones: Improvement in survival and tumor volume greater than 25% with TP-317 monotherapy or combination arm compared to placebo or active comparator and identification of biomarkers that correlate with response/non-response preclinically, are clinically significant in PC and are easily assayed in clinical trials. Phase II, Specific Aim 2. ... Phase II, Specific Aim 3."}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7720119/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "title": "Unbiased in vivo preclinical evaluation of anticancer drugs identifies ...", "date": "2020-11-16", "text": "Among 57 drug conditions screened, combined inhibition of heat shock protein (Hsp)-90 and MEK was found to produce robust suppression of tumor growth, leading to an 80% increase in the survival of PDAC-bearing mice with no significant toxicity. ... () A waterfall representation of the average response of PDAC orthotopic transplants following a 2-wk treatment with the indicated monotherapies. Note that none of the drugs caused tumor regression (mean ± SEM; = 4 per group; * < 0.05, ** < 0.01; one-way ANOVA). ... None of the 16 monotherapies elicited a notable tumor regression following 2 wk of drug administration using concentrations identified in previously published literature (Fig. 1*C*). However, several drugs, including gemcitabine (GEM), trametinib, a MAPK/ERK kinase (MEK)-1/2 inhibitor, and PU-H71, a heat-shock protein (HSP)-90 inhibitor with specificity for tumor HSP90 variants (11–14), significantly reduced tumor growth when compared to control. ... |CDK4/6|Palbociclib|50|QD|p.o.|Sodium lactate buffer (50 mM, pH 4.0)| |Microtubule inhibitor|Abraxane|30|1x/week|i.p.|Saline| |PI3K|Alpelisib|50|QD|i.p.|1% (wt/vol) Carboxymethylcellulose (CMC)+0.5% (wt/vol) Tween 80| |RTK|Sunitinib|40|QD|p.o.|0.5% Carboxy-methylcellulose, ph3.5| |JAK1/2|Ruxolitinib|60|QD|p.o.|0.1% Tween 80| |HSP90|PU-H71|75|3x/week|p.o.|Phosphate buffer| |EGFR|Erlotinib|25|QD|p.o.|0.5% methylcellulose| ... |DNA|Gemcitabine|400|1x/week|i.p.|Saline| |MEK1/2|Trametinib|2|QD|p.o.|0.5% HPMC+0.2%Tween 80| |Src|Dasatinib|30|BID|p.o.|80 mM sodium citrate pH 3.1| ... In contrast, the T/P combination was highly effective at impairing tumor growth and produced a significant survival benefit, extending the median survival of mice by 1.8-fold over control (83 d vs. 46 d, *P* < 0.001, Fig. 2*C*)."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://cdn.clinicaltrials.gov/large-docs/99/NCT03814499/Prot_SAP_000.pdf", "domain": "cdn.clinicaltrials.gov", "title": "�", "date": null, "text": "� ������������������������������ ... ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������"}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://academic.oup.com/view-large/figure/573834660/oyag337f5.tif?itm_medium=graphical+abstract+image&itm_content=open+image&itm_source=http://academic.oup.com/oncolo/advance-article/doi/10.1093/o