the website is restricted for regulatory reasons."}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://onco.cc/regulatory/", "domain": "onco.cc", "title": "Regulatory timeline - OnCo", "date": null, "text": "|29 Oct 2021|AsciminibFDA 2026-09-22 Small-molecule allosteric ABL1 inhibitor (STAMP)|Accelerated approval|US|Adult patients with Philadelphia chromosome-positive chronic myeloid leukemia (Ph+ CML) in chronic phase (CP), previously treated with 2 or more tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs)Accelerated approval on a surrogate endpoint, with a confirmatory trial required.|"}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://www.cancer.gov/publications/dictionaries/cancer-drug/def/wt1-a10-as01b-immunotherapeutic-gsk2130579a", "domain": "cancer.gov", "title": "NCI Drug Dictionary", "date": null, "text": "NCI Dictionaries ... You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://www.nbfira.org.bw/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/nbfira-annual-report-2024.pdf", "domain": "nbfira.org.bw", "title": "ANNUAL REPORT - nbfira.org.bw", "date": null, "text": "The rating is an improvement from the medium high rating recorded during the 2017 assessment."}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://www.delveinsight.com/report-store/acute-myeloid-leukemia-aml-market", "domain": "delveinsight.com", "title": "Acute Myeloid Leukemia Market Summary", "date": "2026-06-01", "text": "|**BP1001**|Interim safety and efficacy of BP1001 in a Phase II acute myeloid leukemia (AML) study.|6511|- Total evaluable- Number of partial remission: 1 (5%), number of stable disease: 3 (15%) - Total enrolled- Number of partial remission: 1 (4%), number of stable disease: 3 (11%) - In relapsed/refractory, among enrolled patients, median survival was 5.7 months. Among evaluable patients, median survival was 5.9 months| |"}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 6483, "cached_input_tokens": 5547, "output_tokens": 628}, "timing": {"search_ms": 459.9, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 7458.8, "total_ms": 79