{"row_id": "q045", "objective": "BMF-500 first regulatory approval or market launch year in acute myeloid leukemia", "anchors": ["BMF-500"], "facet": "catalysts", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 11301, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/0e8fac2d50284b9fac3c91177d16d79c", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "BMF-500 - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents", "date": null, "text": "|Active Indication Acute Myeloid Leukemia| ... |Drug Highest PhasePhase 1| |First Approval Date-| ... |--|--|--|--|--| |Acute Myeloid Leukemia|Phase 1|United States|Biomea Fusion, Inc.|26 Jul 2023|"}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/ix?doc=/Archives/edgar/data/0001840439/000095017024118366/bmea-20240930.htm", "domain": "sec.gov", "title": "Loading Inline Form.", "date": null, "text": "In January 2022, we announced that we had initiated dosing in COVALENT-101, a Phase 1 clinical trial to explore the safety and efficacy of icovamenib in patients with relapsed/refractory AML and acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL), including those with MLL/KMT2A gene arrangements or NPM1 mutations. ... In December 2023, we reported the achievement of minimal residual disease negativity (MRD-neg) in first complete responder in a participant with AML. ... In May 2022, we announced the nomination of our second development candidate, BMF-500, a third-generation oral covalent small molecule inhibitor of activating mutations of the FMS-like tyrosine kinase 3 (FLT3), which are the most frequent genetic alt eration in AML and are associated with poor prognosis. ... In May 2023, we announced FDA clearance of our IND to study BMF-500 in a Phase 1 study (COVALENT-103) examining safety and efficacy in patients with relapsed or refractory acute leukemia with FLT3 wild-type and FLT3 mutations, including those with MLLr/NPM1 mutations. In October 2023, we announced the first participant had been dosed with BMF-500 in relapsed or refractory acute leukemia. We anticipate that the dose escalation for COVALENT-103 will be completed by year end 2024. ... In addition, our lead product candidate, icovamenib, is in clinical development, and we dosed the first participant with our second product candidate, BMF-500, in October 2023, following clearance of our IND by the FDA in May 2023."}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1840439/000095017024039304/bmea-ex99_1.htm", "domain": "sec.gov", "title": "EX-99.1", "date": null, "text": "In 2023, reported initial topline data from Phase 1 study of BMF-219 in acute myeloid leukemia (AML); continuing to progress COVALENT-101 in liquid tumors, COVALENT-102 in solid tumors and COVALENT-103 (BMF-500) in AML. ... In 2023 BMF-500 entered the clinic as the only covalent FLT3 inhibitor in clinical development.” ... We expect these data will inform potentially registrational studies, which we plan to start in 2025, pending discussions with regulatory authorities. ... • Announced FDA clearance of IND for BMF-500 in COVALENT-103, a Phase 1 study, and started enrollment of Biomea’s novel third generation investigational oral covalent inhibitor of FMS-like tyrosine kinase 3 (FLT3)."}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/organization/26bae87fc714320a3f21ce8509ae5e58", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "Biomea Fusion, Inc.", "date": null, "text": "|Inactive Indication Acute Myeloid Leukemia [+12]| |Drug Highest PhasePhase 2| |First Approval Ctry. / Loc.-| |First Approval Date-| BMF-500 |Target FLT3| ... |Active Indication Acute Myeloid Leukemia| |Inactive Indication-| |Drug Highest PhasePhase 1| |First Approval Ctry. / Loc.-| |First Approval Date-| ... |BMF-500 ( FLT3 )|Acute Myeloid Leukemia More|Phase 1|"}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1840439/000119312526121825/bmea-20251231.htm", "domain": "sec.gov", "title": "10-K - SEC.gov", "date": null, "text": "We have a limited operating history, limited experience in conducting clinical trials, have not completed the clinical development of any product candidates, have no products approved for commercial sale, and have not generated any revenue, which may make it difficult for you to evaluate our current business and likelihood of success and viability. ... In September 2025, we announced that we received IND clearance from the FDA for BMF-650, and initiated our ongoing Phase I trial in obese, otherwise healthy volunteers. In January 2025, we announced that we plan to conclude our studies exploring icovamenib’s potential in oncology and explore partnerships to further advance our oncology assets, including BMF-500. ... We have not received marketing approval for any product candidate, and we have not generated any revenue from any product sales or other sources since our inception. We do not expect to generate revenue unless or until we successfully complete preclinical and clinical development and obtain regulatory approval of, and then successfully commercialize, at least one product candidate. ... In September 2025, we announced that BMF-650, our investigational, next-generation, oral small molecule GLP-1 RA, received IND-clearance from the FDA. Initiation of our Phase I GLP-131 trial for BMF-650 in obese, otherwise healthy volunteers is ongoing, and data is anticipated in the second quarter of 2026."}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=7dcd09a2-09b0-4543-b9f1-8d95262deb65", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "title": "BMF-500 / Biomea Fusion - LARVOL DELTA", "date": null, "text": "## COVALENT-103: A Phase 1 Study of BMF-500 in Adults With Acute Leukemia (clinicaltrials.gov) - P1 | N=35 | Completed | Sponsor: Biomea Fusion Inc. | Active, not recruiting ➔ Completed | Trial primary completion date: Apr 2026 ➔ Jan 2026 ... ## COVALENT-103: A Phase 1 Study of BMF-500 in Adults With Acute Leukemia (clinicaltrials.gov) - P1 | N=35 | Active, not recruiting | Sponsor: Biomea Fusion Inc. | Recruiting ➔ Active, not recruiting | N=84 ➔ 35 | Trial primary completion date: Jul 2025 ➔ Jan 2026"}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NASDAQ/BMEA/fda-events/?drug=icovamenib&anchor=fda-icovamenib-2026-06-05", "domain": "marketbeat.com", "title": "Biomea Fusion (BMEA) FDA Approvals, PDUFA Dates & Drug Alerts 2026 $BMEA", "date": "2026-06-08", "text": "Given that the GLP-1 receptors in monkeys are functionally similar to those in humans, the findings support further clinical development of BMF-650 as a promising, patient-friendly treatment for obesity.Read Announcement BMF-500 FDA Regulatory Timeline and Events BMF-500 is a drug developed by Biomea Fusion for the following indication: Orally Bioavailable Covalent Inhibitor of FLT3. This drug is under review by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). Below is a timeline of key regulatory milestones for this therapy. Updated data - June 13,2025Updated Data Phase 1Drug: BMF-500Announced Date: June 13, 2025Indication: Orally Bioavailable Covalent Inhibitor of FLT3 AnnouncementBiomea Fusion, Inc. announced updated preliminary clinical data from the ongoing Phase I COVALENT-103 trial of BMF-500 in adults with relapsed or refractory (\"R/R\") acute leukemia (\"AL\"). ... The trial focuses on safety, pharmacokinetics, and early signs of clinical activity in heavily pretreated patients, many with FLT3 mutations. Significant data include bone marrow blast reductions in several patients, with some achieving a complete remission with incomplete hematologic recovery or a morphologic leukemia-free state. ... The study has enrolled 20 patients with relapsed or refractory acute leukemia, including 13 with FLT3 mutations, all of whom had previously failed treatment with gilteritinib. ... In the past two years, Biomea Fusion (BMEA) has not received FDA approval for any therapies. However, the company does have drugs under review or in active clinical development. ... In the past two years, Biomea Fusion (BMEA) has reported FDA regulatory activity for the following drugs: icovamenib, BMF-650, BMF-500, BMF-219 and COVALENT-111."}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://investors.biomeafusion.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biomea-fusion-reports-second-quarter-2025-financial-results-and", "domain": "investors.biomeafusion.com", "title": "Biomea Fusion Reports Second Quarter 2025 Financial ...", "date": "2025-08-05", "text": "**BMF-500 (Oral Small Molecule FLT3 Inhibitor in Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML))** - Presented updated Phase I data at EHA 2025, showing sustained antileukemic responses, deep bone marrow blast reductions, and survival benefit in relapsed/refractory FLT3-mutant AML patients, all of whom had failed FLT3 inhibitor gilteritinib. - The Company concluded its oncology efforts and is now exploring strategic partnerships for BMF-500."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://investors.biomeafusion.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biomea-fusion-announces-fda-clearance-investigational-new-drug-1/", "domain": "investors.biomeafusion.com", "title": "Biomea Fusion Announces FDA Clearance of Investigational New Drug (IND) Application for Covalent FLT3 Inhibitor BMF-500 in Relapsed or Refractory Acute Leukemia | Biomea Fusion", "date": null, "text": "Biomea Fusion Announces FDA Clearance of Investigational New Drug (IND) Application for Covalent FLT3 Inhibitor BMF-500 in Relapsed or Refractory Acute Leukemia - BMF-500, a novel 3rd generation covalent inhibitor of fms-like tyrosine kinase 3 (FLT3), is the second investigational compound, discovered and developed by Biomea’s FUSION™ System, to advance to the clinic. - Phase I study (COVALENT-103) of BMF-500 will examine its safety and efficacy in patients with relapsed or refractory acute leukemia with FLT3 wild-type and FLT3 mutations, including those with MLLr / NPM1 mutations. ... REDWOOD CITY, Calif., May 01, 2023 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Biomea Fusion, Inc. (“Biomea” or “the company”) (Nasdaq: BMEA), a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company dedicated to discovering and developing novel covalent small molecules to treat and improve the lives of patients with genetically defined cancers and metabolic diseases, today announced that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has cleared the company's Investigational New Drug (IND) application to begin a Phase I trial (COVALENT-103) of BMF-500, an investigational covalent FLT3 inhibitor, in adult patients with relapsed or refractory acute leukemia. ... Any forward-looking statements in this press release are based on our current expectations, estimates and projections only as of the date of this release and are subject to a number of risks and uncertainties that could cause actual results to differ materially and adversely from those set forth in or implied by such forward-looking statements, including the risk that we may encounter delays in preclinical or clinical development, the preparation, filing and clearance of INDs, patient enrollment and in the initiation, conduct and completion of our ongoing and planned clinical trials and other research and development activities."}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://trials.co/clinical-trials-details/-/NCT05918692", "domain": "trials.co", "title": "A Phase 1, Study of BMF-500 in Adults With Acute Leukemia - Clinical Trial for Acute Myeloid Leukemia | NCT05918692 | Trials.co", "date": "2023-04-10", "text": "Study Start Date July 26, 2023 (Actual) Primary Completion Date July 31, 2025 (Anticipated) Study Completion Date July 31, 2026 (Anticipated) ... A Phase 1 first-in-human dose-escalation and dose-expansion study of BMF-500, an oral FLT3 inhibitor, in adult patients with acute leukemia. ... A Phase 1 first-in-human dose-escalation and dose-expansion study of BMF-500, an oral covalent FLT3 inhibitor, in adult patients with acute myeloid leukemia (AML), acute lymphocytic leukemia (ALL) and Acute Mixed-Phenotype Leukemia (MPAL) who may or may not be on Antifungals."}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8502, "cached_input_tokens": 5547, "output_tokens": 1040}, "timing": {"search_ms": 726.1, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 12185.6, "total_ms": 12911.7}, "luna_wall_ms": 12185.6, "cost_usd": {"search": 0.001, "jev": 0.0, "luna": 0.0}, "output": {"has_answer": "yes", "summarized_answer": "Biomea Fusion has not received marketing approval for any product candidate; BMF-500’s first-approval-date field is “-”. [E5][E1]", "confident_score": 0.6, "missing": "BMF-500’s first regulatory approval year and market-launch year are not stated.", "citations": ["E5", "E1"], "next_queries": ["BMF-500 AML approval market launch year"]}, "raw_text": null, "metrics": {"json_valid": true, "has_answer": true, "answer_chars": 129, "confident_score": 0.6, "missing_nothing": false, "missing_empty": false, "n_tags": 2, "invalid_tags": [], "uncited_answer": false, "n_cited_items": 2, "cited_domains": ["sec.gov", "synapse.patsnap.com"], "url_in_answer": false, "search_talk": [], "nonempty_when_no": false, "claim_tokens": 4, "ungrounded_tokens": [], "n_ungrounded": 0, "names_subject": true, "subject_in_cited": true, "next_queries": 1, "next_queries_subject_first": 1}}
{"row_id": "q047", "objective": "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor first regulatory approval or market launch year for acute myeloid leukemia", "anchors": ["Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor", "CDK12"], "facet": "catalysts", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 5381, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://insilico.com/news", "domain": "insilico.com", "title": "Press Releases", "date": null, "text": "20 October 2023 Insilico Medicine nominates novel CDK12/13 small molecule inhibitor as preclinical candidate for multiple tumors"}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://insilico.com/pipeline_target_cdk12/13", "domain": "insilico.com", "title": "CDK12/13", "date": null, "text": "Cyclin-dependent kinase 12/13 (CDK12/13) Inhibitor: Treating Tumors through Induction of BRCAness (IND-Enabling) Assays Completed Wholly-owned and Available for Licensing - *In vivo* efficacy studies – Combo study with Olaparib and Cisplatin - *In vivo* efficacy studies – Single agent - *In vivo* PK-PD - *In vivo* PK studies - *In vitro* ADMET studies - Developability/CMC - *In vitro* cell-based - Toxicology studies - Enzymatic ... Insilico Medicine CDK12 Inhibitor Summary – IND-Enabling ... Effective in both mono and combo therapies ... - Potential broader indications such as AML, HCC, SCLC, Colorectal cancer, and Ovarian cancer ... *In vivo* efficacy studies in SUM149PT CDX mice models showed strong dose-dependent anti-tumor activity with robust and durable tumor regression."}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://siliconvalleyinvestclub.com/companies/insilico/tear-sheet.pdf", "domain": "siliconvalleyinvestclub.com", "title": "Insilico Medicine", "date": null, "text": "Insilico Medicine nominates novel CDK12/13 small molecule inhibitor as preclinical candidate for multiple tumors"}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://colab.ws/articles/10.1021%2Facs.jmedchem.4c01616", "domain": "colab.ws", "title": "Design, Synthesis, and Biological Evaluation of Novel Orally ...", "date": "2025-02-22", "text": "Here, we report the discovery of compound 12b as a novel, potent, orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitor with a promising safety profile and robust in vivo antitumor properties."}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://www.eurekalert.org/news-releases/1074881", "domain": "eurekalert.org", "title": "JMC｜With generative AI assistance, Insilico Medicine ...", "date": "2025-02-26", "text": "Insilico Medicine (\"Insilico\"), a clinical stage generative artificial intelligence (AI)-driven biotechnology company, today announced the publication of a novel series of orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitors, as a potential option against refractory and treatment-resistant cancers. Published in the ***Journal of Medicinal Chemistry* ** (IF=7.2), the study showcases the discovery of compound 12b, a potent, selective, and safe therapy targeting CDK12/13, empowered by Insilico’s proprietary generative AI platforms including PandaOmics and Chemistry42. ... During the preclinical *in vitro* and *in vivo* testing, compound 12b demonstrated nanomolar potencies across cancer cell lines, desirable ADME properties. Furthermore, 12b exhibited significant efficacy in breast cancer and acute myeloid leukemia (AML) models, all without inducing intolerable side effects, paving the way for further therapeutic development. ... \"The research and development process showcases how AI-guided drug design can achieve both precision and safety in cancer therapeutics, and we are striving to advance the compound in this program into clinical trials in the near future.\""}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://sigma.larvol.com/moa.php?MoaId=777818&tab=newstrac", "domain": "sigma.larvol.com", "title": "CDK12 inhib News", "date": "2025-06-13", "text": "Here, we report the discovery of compound 12b as a novel, potent, orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitor with a promising safety profile and robust in vivo antitumor properties."}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://sigma.larvol.com/company.php?CompanyId=968423&tab=newstrac", "domain": "sigma.larvol.com", "title": "Insilico Medicine News", "date": "2025-05-25", "text": "Results from a 28-day rat DRF study revealed that the compound did not show evident signs of toxicity at the tested doses, suggesting a reasonable safety window for ISM6466A.In summary, the novel, covalent, small-molecule CDK12 inhibitor, ISM6466A, demonstrated excellent preclinical efficacy along with favorable drug-like properties. Our results underscore the therapeutic potential of ISM6466A for the treatment of cancer."}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://insilico.com/mediakit", "domain": "insilico.com", "title": "Media Kit", "date": null, "text": "Insilico Medicine (\"Insilico\") is a global, clinical stage, end-to-end, generative artificial intelligence (AI)-driven biotech company responsible for advancing the first generative AI-discovered and generative AI-designed drug to human clinical trials."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/in-silico-medicine_design-synthesis-and-biological-evaluation-activity-7296190298206973952-MIOC", "domain": "linkedin.com", "title": "Insilico Medicine's Post - LinkedIn", "date": "2025-02-14", "text": "Here, we report the discovery of compound 12b as a novel, potent, orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitor with a promising safety profile and robust in vivo antitumor properties."}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/d4f56c4afbbf4e43805fc7050386be8a", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "title": "CDK12/13 TARGET therapy (InSilico Medicine) - Patsnap Synapse", "date": "2025-05-08", "text": "CDK12/13 TARGET therapy (InSilico Medicine) ... Target CDK12 x CDK13 Action inhibitors Mechanism CDK12 inhibitors(cyclin dependent kinase 12 inhibitors), CDK13 inhibitors(cyclin dependent kinase 13 inhibitors) Therapeutic Areas Neoplasms Active Indication Solid tumor ... Originator Organization InSilico Medicine Hong Kong Ltd. ... Drug Highest Phase Preclinical First Approval Date ... China InSilico Medicine Hong Kong Ltd. 11 Jun 2024"}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7004, "cached_input_tokens": 5547, "output_tokens": 493}, "timing": {"search_ms": 573.3, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 6554.5, "total_ms": 7127.8}, "luna_wall_ms": 6554.5, "cost_usd": {"search": 0.001, "jev": 0.0, "luna": 0.0}, "output": {"has_answer": "no", "summarized_answer": "", "missing": "The first regulatory approval or market launch year for the Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor in acute myeloid leukemia.", "citations": [], "next_queries": ["Dual CDK12/13 inhibitor acute myeloid leukemia approval market launch"]}, "raw_text": null, "metrics": {"json_valid": true, "has_answer": false, "answer_chars": 0, "confident_score": null, "missing_nothing": false, "missing_empty": false, "n_tags": 0, "invalid_tags": [], "uncited_answer": false, "n_cited_items": 0, "cited_domains": [], "url_in_answer": false, "search_talk": [], "nonempty_when_no": false, "claim_tokens": 0, "ungrounded_tokens": [], "n_ungrounded": 0, "names_subject": false, "subject_in_cited": false, "next_queries": 1, "next_queries_subject_first": 1}}
{"row_id": "q048", "objective": "dCASP1-55 first regulatory approval or market launch year in acute myeloid leukemia", "anchors": ["dCASP1-55"], "facet": "catalysts", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 13642, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://cdas.cancer.gov/approved-projects/5003/", "domain": "cdas.cancer.gov", "title": "Internal Server Error", "date": null, "text": "Please contact the server administrator at webcontacts@imsweb.com to inform them of the time this error occurred, and the actions you performed just before this error."}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://www.cstonepharma.com/en/news/company_news16.html", "domain": "cstonepharma.com", "title": "Press Release-CStone Pharmaceuticals", "date": "2021-03-01", "text": "Select “Accept all” for giving your consent to all cookies or select “Reject all” for using only strictly necessary cookies."}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://www.uc.edu/news/articles/2024/12/aml-sickle-cell-disease-research-among-uc-ash-abstract-highlights.html", "domain": "uc.edu", "title": "AML, sickle cell disease research among highlights of ASH abstracts", "date": "2024-12-10", "text": "A randomized Phase 1 trial in healthy volunteers found a new drug targeting treatment-resistant acute myeloid leukemia (AML) is safe and attains drug levels that would predict response in this disease. ... Lomonitinib is now being tested in Phase 1B trials in Australia and in the United States as part of the Beat AML master trial. It is expected that the lomonitinib trial will open at the University of Cincinnati Cancer Center in early 2025."}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://www.cstonepharma.com/en/relation/notice15.html", "domain": "cstonepharma.com", "title": "Circulars & Announcements-CStone Pharmaceuticals", "date": "2025-01-01", "text": "Select “Accept all” for giving your consent to all cookies or select “Reject all” for using only strictly necessary cookies."}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://aml-hub.com/search", "domain": "aml-hub.com", "title": "Search | AML Hub", "date": "2026-09-29", "text": "The AML Hub is an independent medical education platform, sponsored by Daiichi Sankyo, Kura Oncology, Syndax, Abbvie, Thermo Fisher and Johnson & Johnson."}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://med.uc.edu/research/clinicaltrials?strDept=All&query=&page=13", "domain": "med.uc.edu", "title": "Clinical Trials - College of Medicine - University of Cincinnati", "date": null, "text": "A Phase 1b Study of Menin Inhibitor SNDX-5613 in Combination with Daunorubicin and Cytarabine in Newly Diagnosed Patients with Acute Myeloid Leukemia and NPM1 Mutated/FLT3 Wildtype with Higher-Risk Features or MLL/KMT2A Rearranged Disease. This phase Ib trial evaluates the safety, side effects, and optimal dosage of SNDX-5613 in combination with standard chemotherapy (daunorubicin and cytarabine) for patients with newly diagnosed acute myeloid leukemia (AML) harboring NPM1 or MLL/KMT2A gene mutations."}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://www.dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/getArchivalFile.cfm?archive_id=861973", "domain": "dailymed.nlm.nih.gov", "title": "��x���mE��8�Y\"�ɒ^�����QrW��0.�7�*�4�2� ���J��w�in�QM����!���c,��0��|���2^�P���x�ߖ73�� ��y.�]���4ي� i�����w��U�»ut��<�n��,*�e��Y��CA6�gx��R7;q6��V��=��D�/UH�}F�耔�䌶��br.����B8m�6�c ��-�u��Le�!foS|���Ć�t�(c$�KX����C,�zN: $ t�78qu�4��,?����( M�/��Q�����S�L�M���1�?M}�-���k���*h�3A���4avy�a���^6��^]���\"�����SM7͋:�x_�.�j�V�[������Ec��Rغ<9m���խz��j�=����w'%�q�H��������\\��+��� ���$h�[m�������Mx�RC�Ky, T�Õ�S��o7��ԩ���]� LѤ�j1&dފ��h�-+��YRO�GT��,����F�*АG��~��mhm���5l��x�?|��[d� ��~��RM���zt1_h�.r�v���]�C� �N;�f3ps��\\��f _���'�|\\GR�r��O�a�Z��+dz���`�� z��\\s��e��vҜk��J9��,Hi ���_ v�%ʐ���b�j�j�mh�UU�4��<�s�pZ��qZ.1�iaM�?/unԦ�7��\\��u'2��� �m��mr�v�33�uW�鬔���-d;a3�`{��WouS��5����C*��6�У��l^�D�ʢՏ$Xf�L�߃Q?�|V^��+��L����| ��|.b\\��o��l�:sbD�ܖ�nK�k[d�Ⱦ��b^Jy�/k��W���� �<�?E8 ���, ��Q�?@�I�i @������k|>��ii�d_�7{�U��7�^9�u�wpG+�c�f|D$(�4VUՊl��hu���/���+������+����exӉ&v>�s`o�i3