{"row_id": "q056", "objective": "MNPS Asset planned or expected data readouts, regulatory submissions, regulatory decisions, and expected timing in Head and Neck Cancer", "anchors": ["MNPS"], "facet": "catalysts", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 9866, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://cdas.cancer.gov/approved-projects/5003/", "domain": "cdas.cancer.gov", "title": "Internal Server Error", "date": null, "text": "Please contact the server administrator at webcontacts@imsweb.com to inform them of the time this error occurred, and the actions you performed just before this error."}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://hpr-rps.hres.ca/reg-content/regulatory-decision-summary.php", "domain": "hpr-rps.hres.ca", "title": "Search Page - Drug and Health Product Register", "date": "2014-10-23", "text": "## Regulatory Decision Summary Search All Regulatory Decision Summaries - **Date modified:** 2016-04-13"}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://www.miragenews.com/tag/head-and-neck-cancer/", "domain": "miragenews.com", "title": "Live Head And Neck Cancer updates", "date": "2026-10-02", "text": "Live Head And Neck Cancer news coverage of developments with the latest updates."}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://www.law360.com/subscribe/free_trial?target_url=https://www.law360.com/companies/molecular-pathology-laboratory-network-inc/articles", "domain": "law360.com", "title": "Legal News & Analysis on Litigation, Policy, Deals : Law360", "date": "2026-09-30", "text": "Legal News & Analysis on Litigation, Policy, Deals : Law360 ... ## Sign up now for free access to this content"}, {"id": "E5", "url": "https://datalookout.com/head-neck-cancer-clinical-trials", "domain": "datalookout.com", "title": "Nasopharyngeal Carcinoma...", "date": null, "text": "The checkpoint immunotherapy era transformed recurrent/metastatic HNSCC: pembrolizumab (Keytruda) is FDA-approved as first-line monotherapy for high CPS scores and in combination with chemotherapy for all-comers; nivolumab (Opdivo) is approved in platinum-refractory disease. ... |NCT06589804|Cetuximab + pembrolizumab vs pembrolizumab in 2L+ relapsed/metastatic HNSCC|National Cancer Institute (NCI)|Recruiting| ... |NCT07026474|Re-chemoradiotherapy + pembrolizumab vs immunotherapy alone for locoregional recurrence (PD-L1 CPS≥1)|Universität des Saarlandes|Recruiting| ... Merus subsequently launched two Phase 3 registrational trials covering the two most commercially significant HNSCC settings: - **LiGeR-HN1 (NCT06525220):** Petosemtamab + pembrolizumab vs pembrolizumab in first-line R/M HNSCC. This is the pivotal trial for the 1L commercial indication, competing directly with pembrolizumab + chemotherapy standard of care."}, {"id": "E6", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0385814623001402", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "title": "[PDF] 2022 Update edited by the Japan Society for Head and Neck Cancer", "date": null, "text": "If you are unable to access your content please try accessing the content again or contact our support team"}, {"id": "E7", "url": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/hed.28211", "domain": "onlinelibrary.wiley.com", "title": "First-Line Therapy in Recurrent or Metastatic Head and Neck Squamous Cell Carcinoma: A Retrospective, Multicenter, Real-World Study", "date": "2025-11-01", "text": "# First-Line Therapy in Recurrent or Metastatic Head and Neck Squamous Cell Carcinoma: A Retrospective, Multicenter, Real-World Study ... In Europe, pembrolizumab with or without chemotherapy is the recommended first-line treatment for recurrent or metastatic head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (R/M HNSCC), with a combined positive score (CPS) ≥ 1. In France, the TPExtreme (TPEx) regimen is preferred for CPS < 1. ... We reviewed all R/M HNSCC cases treated with first-line regimens between January 2021 and December 2023 in Nancy and Lille. Data on patient history, treatments, survival, response, and safety were collected. ... The analysis included 290 patients; 19% received pembrolizumab alone, 28% received pembrolizumab with chemotherapy, 19% received TPEx, and 20% received adapted regimens. PFS and OS differed significantly between groups. Median PFS and OS were respectively 2.9 and 9.4 months for pembrolizumab, 6 and 15.5 months for pembrolizumab-chemotherapy, 5.9 and 13.7 months for TPEx, and 4.3 and 10 months for adapted regimens. Pembrolizumab alone is the safest regimen. ... This retrospective study reflects real-world first-line therapy for R/M HNSCC in two French cancer institutes. Pembrolizumab combined with chemotherapy is the preferred treatment option. ... Historically, the first-line treatment for recurrent or metastatic head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (R/M HNSCC) has been chemotherapy alone. ... The European Society for Medical Oncology (ESMO) recommends [9] the use of pembrolizumab for patients with a CPS ≥ 1, potentially associated with chemotherapy, and the EXTREME or TPEx regimens for patients with a CPS < 1. These recommendations apply only to patients in good health condition. ... This retrospective, multicentric study included patients treated for R/M HNSCC from January 1st 2021 to December 31th 2023, in Nancy (ICL) and Lille (COL). ... Between January 1, 2021 and December 31, 2023, 290 patients treated for R/M HNSCC were included: 157 (54%) in ICL and 133 (46%) in COL. ... ORR was 18% in the pembrolizumab group (10 patients, with 1 complete response at 2–12 months), 57.5% in the pembrolizumab-chemotherapy group (46 patients, with 1 complete response at 2–12 months), 59% in the TPEx group (33 patients), and 39% in the adapted regimens group (23 patients, 2 complete responses at 2 and 4 months). ... PFS differed significantly between groups, with a median PFS of 2.9 months [95% CI 2.1–3.7] for pembrolizumab, 6 [4.7–7.4] for pembrolizumab-chemotherapy, 5.9 [4.3–7.4] for TPEx, and 4.3 [3.2–5.4] for adapted regimens (Figure 1). ... Pembrolizumab, alone or in combination with chemotherapy, is favored for patients with a CPS ≥ 1, while the TPEx regimen remains common for patients with a CPS < 1."}, {"id": "E8", "url": "https://www.cancernetwork.com/clinical/head-neck-cancer", "domain": "cancernetwork.com", "title": "Head & Neck Cancer | Clinical - CancerNetwork", "date": "2017-09-15", "text": "The regulatory decision for subcutaneous amivantamab in recurrent/metastatic head and neck squamous cell carcinoma was based on phase 1b/2 OrigAMI-4 data. ... The safety profile of amivantamab was consistent with previous reports in this HNSCC population, with no new signals reported. ... Data from the BL-B01D1-301 study support iza-bren as a potential standard of care for pretreated recurrent or metastatic nasopharyngeal carcinoma. ... The investigator-evaluated ORR was 39.0% among those treated for recurrent/metastatic HNSCC, and the CR and PR rates were 9.8% and 29.3%, respectively."}, {"id": "E9", "url": "https://powerfulpatients.org/no/2020/10/20/head-and-neck-cancers/", "domain": "powerfulpatients.org", "title": "An error occurred.", "date": "2020-10-20", "text": "Please try again later. If you see this error constantly and you are the system administrator of this resource then please make sure that you are not blocking our IP address: 51.178.160.40"}, {"id": "E10", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13101959/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "title": "Driving Progress in Recurrent and Metastatic Head and Neck Cancer", "date": "2026-07-01", "text": "The KEYNOTE-048 study^8^ established the use of pembrolizumab in the first-line setting, either as monotherapy (limited to patients with PD-L1 ≥ 1 expression) or in combination with platinum and 5-fluorouracil (5-FU). As a result, immunotherapy was established as the core element of standard-of-care in the first-line treatment of platinum-sensitive R/M HNSCC. The updated results from this study with a median follow-up of 45 months have shown an improved median OS in the pembrolizumab group compared to chemotherapy in the CPS ≥ 20 (14.9 vs 10.8 months; HR 0.61; 95% CI 0.46–0.81) and CPS ≥ 1 populations (12.3 vs 10.4 months; HR 0.74; 95% CI 0.61–0.89)^14^. Also the combination of pembrolizumab-chemotherapy group compared to chemotherapy alone demonstrated a benefit in median OS in the PD-L1 CPS ≥ 20 (14.7 vs 11.1 months; HR 0.62; 95% CI 0.46–0.84), CPS ≥ 1 (13.6 vs 10.6 months; ... The phase 4 study KEYNOTE-B10^15^ was a non-randomized, single arm study with ORR reaching 49% in the overall population. Despite the inherent differences between real-world populations and clinical trial cohorts, pembrolizumab-based regimens have shown comparable OS results in the real-world population to previously demonstrated in the KEYNOTE-048 trial^16,17^. ... Despite biological^10^ and technical limitations, PD-L1 remains a dominant factor to guiding first-line treatment decision. Tumor heterogeneity, including intrapatient variability across primary and metastatic sites, and fixed cutoff thresholds challenges its reproducibility and standardization across studies and clinical settings. ... Retrospective analyses have demonstrated no statistically significant difference in survival outcomes between patients who discontinued versus continued immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy at one- or two-year timepoints^55^. ... Preliminary results demonstrated an ORR of around 32% in the first-line setting for patients with PD-L1 CPS ≥1^58^. ... Undetectable ctDNA levels following an initial response may help identify patients in whom treatment can be safely de-escalated or discontinued, while persistent ctDNA may indicate the need for continued therapy. ... Immune checkpoint blockade with different agents such as nivolumab, pembrolizumab or toripalimab paired with EGFR inhibitors have demonstrated overall response rates (ORR) ranging from 30% to 55% in immune-naïve populations^86,87,88,89^. ... Petosentamab (MCLA-158), a bispecific antibody that targets the epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) and the leucine-rich repeat containing G-protein-coupled receptor 5 (LGR5), currently holds two breakthrough therapy designations by the FDA for patients with R/M HNSCC who have experienced disease progression following treatment with platinum-based chemotherapy and a PD-L1/PD-1 inhibitor^91^ and also in the first-line setting in combination with pembrolizumab for patients with PD-L1 (CPS≥1)^92^. The combination of petosentamab with pembrolizumab continues to be investigated in the ..."}], "ok": true, "error": null, "status": 200, "attempts": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8187, "cached_input_tokens": 5547, "output_tokens": 263}, "timing": {"search_ms": 561.1, "jev_ms": 0.0, "luna_ms": 5153.0, "total_ms": 5714.1}, "luna_wall_ms": 5153.0, "cost_usd": {"search": 0.001, "jev": 0.0, "luna": 0.0}, "output": {"has_answer": "no", "summarized_answer": "", "missing": "MNPS-specific planned or expected data readouts, regulatory submissions, regulatory decisions, and their expected timing in head and neck cancer.", "citations": [], "next_queries": ["MNPS head and neck cancer data readout", "MNPS head and neck cancer regulatory submission", "MNPS head and neck cancer regulatory decision", "MNPS head and neck cancer milestones timeline"]}, "raw_text": null, "metrics": {"json_valid": true, "has_answer": false, "answer_chars": 0, "confident_score": null, "missing_nothing": false, "missing_empty": false, "n_tags": 0, "invalid_tags": [], "uncited_answer": false, "n_cited_items": 0, "cited_domains": [], "url_in_answer": false, "search_talk": [], "nonempty_when_no": false, "claim_tokens": 0, "ungrounded_tokens": [], "n_ungrounded": 0, "names_subject": false, "subject_in_cited": false, "next_queries": 4, "next_queries_subject_first": 4}}
{"row_id": "q057", "objective": "CNP200137 first regulatory approval or market launch year for acute myeloid leukemia", "anchors": ["CNP200137"], "facet": "catalysts", "scope": null, "skip": null, "abstained": false, "n_items": 10, "evidence_chars": 3186, "evidence": [{"id": "E1", "url": "https://www.inflectionlabs.bio/reports/menin-inhibitor-pipeline", "domain": "inflectionlabs.bio", "title": "Menin Inhibitor Drug Development Pipeline: AML, Diabetes ...", "date": null, "text": "**3. CNP200137 (CoBX Bio, Pharos iBio)** This is a pre-clinical stage, next-generation menin inhibitor that is designed to address menin resistance challenges.^[58]^ CNP200137 may well be the same molecule as CXB-001 with a different name, or a completely separate molecule being developed by the same South Korean biotech partnership.^[59]^"}, {"id": "E2", "url": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/oncology-cancerhematologic-malignancies-approval-notifications", "domain": "fda.gov", "title": "Oncology (Cancer)/Hematologic Malignancies Approval ...", "date": "2026-09-24", "text": "venetoclax for newly diagnosed acute myeloid leukemia|On May 13, 2026, the Food and Drug Administration approved an oral combination of decitabine and cedazuridine tablets (Inqovi, Taiho Oncology, Inc.) with venetoclax for the treatment of newly diagnosed acute myeloid leukemia (AML) in adults 75 years or older, or who have comorbidities that preclude the use of intensive induction chemotherapy.|5/13/2026|"}, {"id": "E3", "url": "https://2npharma.com/category/press-releases/page/4", "domain": "2npharma.com", "title": "555 Security Incident Detected", "date": null, "text": "You can see the detailed reason for this in your webserver logs."}, {"id": "E4", "url": "https://www.q-depot.com/blog/cnp-laboratory", "domain": "q-depot.com", "title": "520: Web server is returning an unknown error", "date": null, "text": "Please include the Ray ID (which is at the bottom of this error page)."}, {"id": 